  ["traphazard.wild-magic-zone.xdmg2024"]={title="Wild Magic Zone",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 69\n\nA past magical disaster or uncontrolled surge of power in a particular place can cause the fabric of magic to unravel, creating a wild magic zone. In such an area, which is typically no more than 300 feet in diameter, magic behaves unpredictably.\n\nWhenever a creature expends a spell slot to cast a spell in a wild magic zone, roll 1d20. If you roll a 20 on the die, roll on the XPHB table in the XPHB to create a magical effect."},
  ["feature.wild-resurgence.xphb2024.druid.base.5"]={title="Wild Resurgence",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.wild-shape.phb2014.druid.base.2"]={title="Wild Shape",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your action to magically assume the shape of a beast that you have seen before. You can use this feature twice. You regain expended uses when you finish a short or long rest.\n\nYour druid level determines the beasts you can transform into, as shown in the Beast Shapes table. At 2nd level, for example, you can transform into any beast that has a challenge rating of 1/4 or lower that doesn't have a flying or swimming speed.\n\nLevel | Max. CR | Limitations | Example\n\n2nd | bestiary | No flying or swimming speed | Wolf\n\n4th | bestiary | No flying speed | Crocodile\n\n8th | bestiary | — | Giant eagle\n\nYou can stay in a beast shape for a number of hours equal to half your druid level (rounded down). You then revert to your normal form unless you expend another use of this feature. You can revert to your normal form earlier by using a bonus action on your turn. You automatically revert if you fall unconscious, drop to 0 hit points, or die.\n\nWhile you are transformed, the following rules apply:\n\n• Your game statistics are replaced by the statistics of the beast, but you retain your alignment, personality, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. You also retain all of your skill and saving throw proficiencies, in addition to gaining those of the creature. If the creature has the same proficiency as you and the bonus in its stat block is higher than yours, use the creature's bonus instead of yours. If the creature has any legendary or lair actions, you can't use them.\n\n• When you transform, you assume the beast's hit points and Hit Dice. When you revert to your normal form, you return to the number of hit points you had before you transformed. However, if you revert as a result of dropping to 0 hit points, any excess damage carries over to your normal form. For example, if you take 10 damage in animal form and have only 1 hit point left, you revert and take 9 damage. As long as the excess damage doesn't reduce your normal form to 0 hit points, you aren't knocked unconscious.\n\n• You can't cast spells, and your ability to speak or take any action that requires hands is limited to the capabilities of your beast form. Transforming doesn't break your concentration on a spell you've already cast, however, or prevent you from taking actions that are part of a spell, such as call lightning, that you've already cast.\n\n• You retain the benefit of any features from your class, race, or other source and can use them if the new form is physically capable of doing so. However, you can't use any of your special senses, such as darkvision, unless your new form also has that sense.\n\n• You choose whether your equipment falls to the ground in your space, merges into your new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal, but the DM decides whether it is practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment, based on the creature's shape and size. Your equipment doesn't change size or shape to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can't wear must either fall to the ground or merge with it. Equipment that merges with the form has no effect until you leave the form."},
  ["feature.wild-shape.xphb2024.druid.base.2"]={title="Wild Shape",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.wild-shape-improvement.phb2014.druid.base.4"]={title="Wild Shape Improvement",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nAt 4th level, your Wild Shape improves as shown on the Beast Shapes table."},
  ["feature.wild-shape-improvement.phb2014.druid.base.8"]={title="Wild Shape Improvement",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nAt 8th level, your Wild Shape improves as shown on the Beast Shapes table."},
  ["feature.wild-surge.tce2014.barbarian.wild-magic.3"]={title="Wild Surge",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\n3rd-level Path of Wild Magic feature\n\nThe magical energy roiling inside you sometimes erupts from you. When you enter your rage, roll on the Wild Magic table to determine the magical effect produced.\n\nIf the effect requires a saving throw, the DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier.\n\nd8 | Magical Effect\n\n1 | Shadowy tendrils lash around you. Each creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d12 necrotic damage. You also gain 1d12 temporary hit points.\n\n2 | You teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again on each of your turns as a bonus action.\n\n3 | An intangible spirit, which looks like a flumph or a pixie (your choice), appears within 5 feet of one creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you. At the end of the current turn, the spirit explodes, and each creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d6 force damage. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again, summoning another spirit, on each of your turns as a bonus action.\n\n4 | Magic infuses one weapon of your choice that you are holding. Until your rage ends, the weapon's damage type changes to force, and it gains the light and thrown properties, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If the weapon leaves your hand, the weapon reappears in your hand at the end of the current turn.\n\n5 | Whenever a creature hits you with an attack roll before your rage ends, that creature takes 1d6 force damage, as magic lashes out in retribution.\n\n6 | Until your rage ends, you are surrounded by multi colored, protective lights; you gain a +1 bonus to AC, and while within 10 feet of you, your allies gain the same bonus.\n\n7 | Flowers and vines temporarily grow around you. Until your rage ends, the ground within 15 feet of you is difficult terrain for your enemies.\n\n8 | A bolt of light shoots from your chest. Another creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d6 radiant damage and be blinded until the start of your next turn. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again on each of your turns as a bonus action."},
  ["creature.wildfire-spirit.tce2014"]={title="Wildfire Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCA: 13\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you speak\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, grappled, prone, restrained\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nFlame Seed\n\nrw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, range 60 ft., one target you can see. h1d6 + PB fire damage.\n\nFiery Teleportation\n\nThe spirit and each willing creature of your choice within 5 feet of it teleport up to 15 feet to unoccupied spaces you can see. Then each creature within 5 feet of the space that the spirit left must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC or take 1d6 + PB fire damage."},
  ["item.wildroot.toa2014"]={title="Wildroot",subtitle="Item - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nIntroducing the juice of a wildroot into a poisoned creature's bloodstream (for example, by rubbing it on an open wound) rids the creature of the poisoned condition. Once used in this way, a wildroot loses this property."},
  ["magicitem.wildspace-orrery.aag2014"]={title="Wildspace Orrery",subtitle="Item Magico - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nInside a Wildspace system, this portable arcane device automatically tracks the positions and movements of all suns, planets, moons, and comets within that system, projecting a display of all these bodies in the space above its current location. In that display, a white, pulsating pinprick of light marks the orrery's location."},
  ["background.wildspacer.aag2014"]={title="Wildspacer",subtitle="Background - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nClose Encounter\n\nYou had a harrowing encounter with one of Wildspace's many terrors. You escaped with your life, but the encounter left you with a scar or two, or perhaps a recurring nightmare. Roll on the Close Encounter table to determine which creature nearly got the best of you. Creatures marked with an asterisk appear in BAM; the others are described in the MM.\n\nd10 | Creature\n\n1 | Beholder\n\n2 | BAM*\n\n3 | BAM*\n\n4 | bestiary*\n\n5 | Mind flayer\n\n6 | BAM*\n\n7 | MPMM*\n\n8 | BAM*\n\n9 | BAM*\n\n10 | BAM*\n\nFeature: Wildspace Adaptation\n\nYou gain the Tough from the PHB. In addition, you learned how to adapt to zero gravity. Being weightless doesn't give you disadvantage on any of your melee attack rolls (see \"AAG\" in AAG)."},
  ["traphazard.wildstorm.nf2014"]={title="Wildstorm",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - NF - 2014",body="Areas of unstable magic can spin into small, translucent tornadoes called wildstorms. A wildstorm fills a 10-foot XPHB. It has a Speed of 50 feet. Each round on Initiative count 0 (losing ties), a wildstorm moves toward the nearest creature and stops in its space. A wildstorm dissipates after 1d4 minutes.\n\nA creature that enters a wildstorm for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there is subjected to a random effect on the Wildstorm Effects table.\n\n1d20 | Effect\n\n1–2 | The wildstorm becomes momentarily incendiary around the creature. The creature takes 2 (1d4) Fire damage and is burning.\n\n3–6 | Shards of magical force whirl past the creature. The creature makes a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 5 (1d10) Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n7–10 | The wildstorm momentarily manifests toxic vapors around the creature. The creature must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or have the XPHB condition for 1 minute. If the creature already has the Poisoned condition, it instead takes 5 (2d4) Poison damage.\n\n11–13 | The creature hears mental cacophony and makes a 12 Wisdom saving throw, taking 5 (1d10) Psychic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. Whether the saving throw succeeds or fails, the creature gains telepathy with a range of 10 feet for 1 minute.\n\n14–17 | The storm renders the creature more susceptible to its other erratic effects. The creature has Vulnerability to Fire, Force, Poison, and Psychic damage for 1 minute.\n\n18–19 | The creature's skin hardens. The creature gains a +2 bonus to AC for 1 minute.\n\n20 | The creature has the XPHB condition for 1 minute."},
  ["creature.wilfred-godefroy.rhw2014"]={title="Wilfred Godefroy",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 142\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 72 (16d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: acid, bludgeoning, cold, fire, lightning, piercing, slashing, thunder\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDarklord Restoration\n\nIf Wilfred dies, he revives with all his XPHB in 1d10 weeks somewhere in Mordent.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nWilfred can move through other creatures and objects as if they were XPHB. He takes 5 (1d10) Force damage if he ends his turn inside an object.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Domain)\n\nIf Wilfred fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nPossessive Aura\n\nGrasping, ghostly servants surround Wilfred in a 5-foot XPHB originating from him. A creature that ends its turn in this area is subjected to the following effect. cha 14. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition. While the creature is XPHB in this way, its XPHB is reduced to 0. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nWilfred makes two attacks, using XPHB Slam or Hunting Rifle in any combination.\n\nObject Slam\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Force damage.\n\nHunting Rifle\n\nr 6, range 40/120 ft. h9 (1d12 + 3) Necrotic damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nRedirect Attack\n\nactTrigger A creature Wilfred can see makes an attack roll against him. actResponse Wilfred chooses a Small or Medium creature within 5 feet of himself that has the XPHB condition. Wilfred and that creature swap places, and the creature becomes the target of the attack instead.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBone-Chilling Step\n\nWilfred teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space he can see, and each creature within 10 feet of the space he left takes 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage. Wilfred can't take this action again until the start of his next turn.\n\nFated Bullet\n\ndex 14, one creature Wilfred can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 16 (2d12 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target can't regain XPHB until the start of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail Wilfred can't take this action again until the start of his next turn.\n\nSlam\n\nWilfred makes one XPHB Slam attack."},
  ["item.will-of-the-talon-awakened.egw2014"]={title="Will of the Talon (Awakened)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.will-of-the-talon-dormant.egw2014"]={title="Will of the Talon (Dormant)",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 279\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nBlack, blue, green, red, and white gems carved in the form of dragon heads cover this ostentatious gold war pick, marking it as a weapon channeling the power of Tiamat.\n\nSentience\n\nWill of the Talon is a sentient lawful evil weapon with an Intelligence of 14, a Wisdom of 15, and a Charisma of 19. It has hearing and darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.\n\nThe weapon communicates telepathically with its wielder and can speak, read, and understand Common, Draconic, and Infernal.\n\nPersonality\n\nA short-tempered bone devil named Ashtyrlon lives within Will of the Talon. The weapon is greedy and values strong leadership. It demands that its wielder take decisive action to keep order in high-pressure situations—and to always take a fair share of treasure in return.\n\nDormant\n\nThe war pick grants the following benefits in its dormant state:\n\n• You can speak, read, and write Draconic and Infernal.\n\n• You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.\n\n• As a bonus action while holding the war pick, you can cause the following effect: each creature of your choice that is within 30 feet of you and is aware of you must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of you for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to your Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours. This property can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\n• While holding the war pick, you can use your action to exhale destructive energy. Pick a damage type from the Will of the Talon Breath Weapons table. Each creature in the area of the exhalation must make a 13 saving throw, the type of which is specified in the table. A creature takes 3d6 damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nWhen you use the war pick to unleash a breath weapon of a specific damage type, you can't choose that same damage type again until the next dawn.\n\nDamage Type | Area | Saving Throw\n\nAcid | 5 ft. wide, 30 ft. long line | Dexterity\n\nCold | 15 ft. cone | Constitution\n\nFire | 15 ft. cone | Dexterity\n\nLightning | 5 ft. wide, 30 ft. long line | Dexterity\n\nPoison | 15 ft. cone | Constitution\n\nBetrayer Artifact Properties\n\nThe Arms of the Betrayers advance in power in the same manner as the Vestiges of Divergence. In its dormant state, each of these artifacts has one dmg property and one dmg property. When the artifact attains an awakened state, it gains an additional dmg property and an additional dmg property. When the item reaches its exalted state, it gains a dmg property. See \"Artifact Properties\" in chapter 7 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for more information."},
  ["item.will-of-the-talon-exalted.egw2014"]={title="Will of the Talon (Exalted)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.will-o-wells.wbtw2014"]={title="Will-o'-Wells",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.will-o-wisp.mm2014"]={title="Will-o'-Wisp",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 301\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / T\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 22 (9d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 50\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 28 | CON 10 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, necrotic, thunder\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nConsume Life\n\nAs a bonus action, the will-o'-wisp can target one creature it can see within 5 feet of it that has 0 hit points and is still alive. The target must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw against this magic or die. If the target dies, the will-o'-wisp regains 10 (3d6) hit points.\n\nEphemeral\n\nThe will-o'-wisp can't wear or carry anything.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe will-o'-wisp can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\nVariable Illumination\n\nThe will-o'-wisp sheds bright light in a 5 to 20-foot radius and dim light for an additional number of ft. equal to the chosen radius. The will-o'-wisp can alter the radius as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShock\n\nms 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h9 (2d8) lightning damage.\n\nInvisibility\n\nThe will-o'-wisp and its light magically become invisible until it attacks or uses its Consume Life, or until its concentration ends (as if concentration on a spell)."},
  ["creature.will-o-wisp.xmm2024"]={title="Will-o'-Wisp",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 333\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / T\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 27 (11d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 50\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 28 | CON 10 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\nResistencias: acid, bludgeoning, cold, fire, necrotic, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEphemeral\n\nThe wisp can't wear or carry anything.\n\nIllumination\n\nThe wisp sheds XPHB in a 20-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 20 feet.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe wisp can move through other creatures and objects as if they were XPHB. It takes 5 (1d10) Force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShock\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d8 + 2) Lightning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nConsume Life\n\ncon 10, one living creature the wisp can see within 5 feet that has 0 XPHB. actSaveFail The target dies, and the wisp regains 10 (3d6) XPHB.\n\nVanish\n\nThe wisp and its light have the XPHB condition until the wisp's XPHB ends on this effect, which ends early immediately after the wisp makes an attack roll or uses Consume Life."},
  ["creature.willifort-crowelle.wdh2014"]={title="Willifort Crowelle",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.willowshade-oil.egw2014"]={title="Willowshade Oil",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 70\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA dark blue oil can be extracted from the rare fruit of the willowshade plant. A creature can use its action to apply the oil to another creature that has been petrified for less than 1 minute, causing the petrified condition on that creature to end at the start of what would be that creature's next turn."},
  ["magicitem.wind-fan.dmg2014"]={title="Wind Fan",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile holding this fan, you can use an action to cast the gust of wind spell (save 13) from it. Once used, the fan shouldn't be used again until the next dawn. Each time it is used again before then, it has a cumulative 20 chance of not working and tearing into useless, nonmagical tatters."},
  ["magicitem.wind-fan.xdmg2024"]={title="Wind Fan",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 325\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile holding this fan, you can cast XPHB (save 13) from it. Each subsequent time the fan is used before the next dawn, it has a cumulative 20 chance of not working; if the fan fails to work, it tears into useless, nonmagical tatters."},
  ["feature.wind-soul.xge2024.sorcerer.storm.18"]={title="Wind Soul",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.wind-speaker.xge2024.sorcerer.storm.1"]={title="Wind Speaker",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["spell.wind-walk.phb2014"]={title="Wind Walk",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 288\n\nYou and up to ten willing creatures you can see within range assume a gaseous form for the duration, appearing as wisps of cloud. While in this cloud form, a creature has a flying speed of 300 feet and has resistance to damage from nonmagical weapons. The only actions a creature can take in this form are the Dash action or to revert to its normal form. Reverting takes 1 minute, during which time a creature is incapacitated and can't move. Until the spell ends, a creature can revert to cloud form, which also requires the 1-minute transformation.\n\nIf a creature is in cloud form and flying when the effect ends, the creature descends 60 feet per round for 1 minute until it lands, which it does safely. If it can't land after 1 minute, the creature falls the remaining distance."},
  ["spell.wind-walk.xphb2024"]={title="Wind Walk",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 341\n\nYou and up to ten willing creatures of your choice within range assume gaseous forms for the duration, appearing as wisps of cloud. While in this cloud form, a target has a XPHB of 300 feet and can hover; it has XPHB to the XPHB condition; and it has XPHB to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage. The only actions a target can take in this form are the XPHB action or a XPHB action to begin reverting to its normal form. Reverting takes 1 minute, during which the target has the XPHB condition. Until the spell ends, the target can revert to cloud form, which also requires a XPHB action followed by a 1-minute transformation.\n\nIf a target is in cloud form and flying when the effect ends, the target descends 60 feet per round for 1 minute until it lands, which it does safely. If it can't land after 1 minute, it falls the remaining distance."},
  ["spell.wind-wall.phb2014"]={title="Wind Wall",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 288\n\nA wall of strong wind rises from the ground at a point you choose within range. You can make the wall up to 50 feet long, 15 feet high, and 1 foot thick. You can shape the wall in any way you choose so long as it makes one continuous path along the ground. The wall lasts for the duration.\n\nWhen the wall appears, each creature within its area must make a Strength saving throw. A creature takes 3d8 bludgeoning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nThe strong wind keeps fog, smoke, and other gases at bay. Small or smaller flying creatures or objects can't pass through the wall. Loose, lightweight materials brought into the wall fly upward. Arrows, bolts, and other ordinary projectiles launched at targets behind the wall are deflected upward and automatically miss. (Boulders hurled by giants or siege engines, and similar projectiles, are unaffected.) Creatures in gaseous form can't pass through it."},
  ["spell.wind-wall.xphb2024"]={title="Wind Wall",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 341\n\nA wall of strong wind rises from the ground at a point you choose within range. You can make the wall up to 50 feet long, 15 feet high, and 1 foot thick. You can shape the wall in any way you choose so long as it makes one continuous path along the ground. The wall lasts for the duration.\n\nWhen the wall appears, each creature in its area makes a Strength saving throw, taking 4d8 Bludgeoning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nThe strong wind keeps fog, smoke, and other gases at bay. Small or smaller flying creatures or objects can't pass through the wall. Loose, lightweight materials brought into the wall fly upward. Arrows, bolts, and other ordinary projectiles launched at targets behind the wall are deflected upward and miss automatically. Boulders hurled by Giants or siege engines, and similar projectiles, are unaffected. Creatures in XPHB can't pass through it."},
  ["creature.windfall.veor2014"]={title="Windfall",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 323 (34d8 + 170)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 24 | CON 20 | INT 22 | WIS 18 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDazzling Visage\n\nA brilliant array of chromatic colors emanates from Windfall, causing attack rolls against her to have disadvantage. This trait ceases to function while Windfall has the incapacitated condition or has a speed of 0.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Windfall fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nWindfall wears an iridescent magic coat that was tailored specifically for her and imbued with Tiamat's power. When she dies, the coat functions as a Robe of Scintillating Colors.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nWindfall makes two Chromatic Rapier attacks and uses Dragon's Fury once.\n\nChromatic Rapier\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (1d8 + 7) piercing damage plus 21 (6d6) acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage (Windfall's choice).\n\nDragon's Fury\n\nWindfall targets one creature she can see within 60 feet of herself and unleashes a burst of magical ire. The target must make a 23 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 36 (8d8) psychic damage and has the frightened condition until the start of Windfall's next turn. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nStunning Scintillation {@recharge 5}\n\nWindfall emits an overwhelming array of colors from her coat. Each creature within 30 feet of Windfall that can see her must succeed on a 23 Constitution saving throw or have the stunned condition until the start of Windfall's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDeft Dance\n\nWindfall moves up to her speed without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nDragon's Flare\n\nWindfall flares with multicolored flames and targets a creature she can see within 30 feet of herself. The target must make a 23 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 26 (4d12) damage of a type chosen by Windfall: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nWindfall uses Spellcasting."},
  ["creature.windharrow.pota2014"]={title="Windharrow",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 55 (10d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 17\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Auran, Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nWindharrow has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put him to sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nWindharrow makes two melee attacks.\n\nRapier\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["magicitem.windskiff.fraif2014"]={title="Windskiff",subtitle="Item Magico - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 247\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis small piece of jewelry has 3 charges and regains all expended charges daily at dawn. While you are holding it, you can take a XPHB action to expend 1 charge, which causes the jewelry to transform into a sail-powered personal vehicle. The vehicle is roughly the size and shape of a household door with a 10-foot-tall sail extending from one side. After 1 hour or until you use the item's command word (no action required), the transformation ends and the Windskiff reverts to its jewelry form.\n\nIn vehicle form, a Windskiff is a Medium object with the following statistics: AC 12, HP 30, and XPHB 40 ft. The Windskiff hovers a few inches above whatever surface it's on and can glide; it moves 5 feet horizontally for every 1 foot it descends in the air. A Windskiff and its riders take no damage from falling."},
  ["magicitem.windvane.pota2014"]={title="Windvane",subtitle="Item Magico - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nA silver spear, Windvane has dark sapphires on the filigreed surface of its polished head. Held by its shining haft, the weapon feels insubstantial, as if clutching a cool, gently flowing breeze. The spear contains a spark of PotA, the Prince of Evil Air.\n\nYou have a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon, which has the finesse weapon property. When you hit with it, the target takes an extra 1d6 lightning damage.\n\nAir Mastery\n\nYou gain the following benefits while you hold Windvane:\n\n• You can speak Auran fluently.\n\n• You have resistance to lightning damage.\n\n• You can cast dominate monster (save 17) on an air elemental. Once you have done so, Windvane can't be used this way again until the next dawn.\n\nSong of the Four Winds\n\nWhile inside an air node, you can perform a ritual called the Song of the Four Winds, using Windvane to create a PotA. Once you perform the ritual, Windvane can't be used to perform the ritual again until the next dawn.\n\nFlaw\n\nWindvane makes its wielder mercurial and unreliable. While attuned to the weapon, you gain the following flaw: \"I break my vows and plans. Duty and honor mean nothing to me.\""},
  ["creature.wine-weird.toa2014"]={title="Wine Weird",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["magicitem.winged-boots.dmg2014"]={title="Winged Boots",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, you have a flying speed equal to your walking speed. You can use the boots to fly for up to 4 hours, all at once or in several shorter flights, each one using a minimum of 1 minute from the duration. If you are flying when the duration expires, you descend at a rate of 30 feet per round until you land.\n\nThe boots regain 2 hours of flying capability for every 12 hours they aren't in use."},
  ["magicitem.winged-boots.xdmg2024"]={title="Winged Boots",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 325\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThese boots have 4 charges and regain 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the boots, you can take a XPHB action to expend 1 charge, gaining a XPHB of 30 feet for 1 hour. If you are flying when the duration expires, you descend at a rate of 30 feet per round until you land."},
  ["creature.winged-bull.mot2014"]={title="Winged Bull",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 95 (10d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 60\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nIdiomas: understands Celestial but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the bull moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 19 (3d12) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (2d12 + 5) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.winged-kobold.mm2014"]={title="Winged Kobold",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 195\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 7 (3d6 - 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 16 | CON 9 | INT 8 | WIS 7 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the kobold has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe kobold has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the kobold's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nDropped Rock\n\nrw 5 to hit, one target directly below the kobold. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.winged-kobold.xmm2024"]={title="Winged Kobold",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 185\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 10 (4d6 - 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 16 | CON 9 | INT 8 | WIS 7 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe kobold has XPHB on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the kobold's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the XPHB condition.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the kobold has XPHB on ability checks and attack rolls.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDragon-Tooth Blade\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\nChromatic Spittle\n\nr 5, range 30 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) damage of a type chosen by the kobold: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison."},
  ["creature.winged-lion.mot2014"]={title="Winged Lion",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 114 (12d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 60\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 14 | CHA 5\n\nIdiomas: understands Celestial but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPounce\n\nIf the lion moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a claw attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the lion can make one bite attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.winged-thrull.ggr2014"]={title="Winged Thrull",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 31 (7d6 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 9 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSelf-Sacrifice\n\nWhen a creature within 5 feet of the thrull is hit by an attack, the thrull swaps places with that creature and is hit instead."},
  ["magicitem.wings-of-flying.dmg2014"]={title="Wings of Flying",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this cloak, you can use an action to speak its command word. This turns the cloak into a pair of bat wings or bird wings on your back for 1 hour or until you repeat the command word as an action. The wings give you a flying speed of 60 feet. When they disappear, you can't use them again for 1d12 hours."},
  ["magicitem.wings-of-flying.xdmg2024"]={title="Wings of Flying",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 324\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this cloak, you can take a XPHB action to turn the cloak into a pair of wings on your back. The wings lasts for 1 hour or until you end the effect early as a XPHB action. The wings give you a XPHB of 60 feet. If you are aloft when the wings disappear, you fall. When the wings disappear, you can't use them again for 1d12 hours."},
  ["feature.wings-unfurled.ftd2014.monk.ascendant-dragon.6"]={title="Wings Unfurled",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\n6th-level Way of the Ascendant Dragon feature\n\nWhen you use your Step of the Wind, you can unfurl spectral draconic wings from your back that vanish at the end of your turn. While the wings exist, you have a flying speed equal to your walking speed.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["magicitem.wingwear.pota2014"]={title="Wingwear",subtitle="Item Magico - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis snug uniform has symbols of air stitched into it and leathery flaps that stretch along the arms, waist, and legs to create wings for gliding. A suit of wingwear has 3 charges. While you wear the suit, you can use a bonus action and expend 1 charge to gain a flying speed of 30 feet until you land. At the end of each of your turns, your altitude drops by 5 feet. Your altitude drops instantly to 0 feet at the end of your turn if you didn't fly at least 30 feet horizontally on that turn. When your altitude drops to 0 feet, you land (or fall), and you must expend another charge to use the suit again.\n\nThe suit regains all of its expended charges after spending at least 1 hour in an elemental air node."},
  ["item.winter-camouflage.frhof2014"]={title="Winter Camouflage",subtitle="Item - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWhile you wear Winter Camouflage in an appropriate environment, you have XPHB on Dexterity (XPHB) checks."},
  ["creature.winter-eladrin.mpmm2014"]={title="Winter Eladrin",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 165 (22d8 + 66)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 16 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 13\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe eladrin has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSorrowful Presence\n\nAny non-eladrin creature that starts its turn within 60 feet of the eladrin must make a 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature becomes charmed by the eladrin for 1 minute. While charmed in this way, the creature has disadvantage on ability checks and saving throws. The charmed creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to any eladrin's Sorrowful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nWhenever the eladrin deals damage to the charmed creature, the charmed creature can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe eladrin makes two Longsword or Longbow attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d8) slashing damage, or 5 (1d10) slashing damage if used with two hands, plus 13 (3d8) cold damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) cold damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nFey Step {@recharge 4}\n\nThe eladrin teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFrigid Rebuke\n\nWhen the eladrin takes damage from a creature the eladrin can see within 60 feet of it, the eladrin can force that creature to make a 16 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 11 (2d10) cold damage."},
  ["creature.winter-eladrin.mtf2014"]={title="Winter Eladrin",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 127 (17d8 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 13\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Step {@recharge 4}\n\nAs a bonus action, the eladrin can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe eladrin has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSorrowful Presence\n\nAny non-eladrin creature that starts its turn within 60 feet of the eladrin must make a 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature is charmed for 1 minute. While charmed in this way, the creature has disadvantage on ability checks and saving throws. The charmed creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to any eladrin's Sorrowful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nWhenever the eladrin deals damage to the charmed creature, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d8) slashing damage, or 5 (1d10) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h4 (1d8) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFrigid Rebuke\n\nWhen the eladrin takes damage from a creature the eladrin can see within 60 feet of it, the eladrin can force that creature to succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or take 11 (2d10) cold damage."},
  ["subclass.winter-walker.frhof2014.ranger.winter-walker.0"]={title="Winter Walker",subtitle="Subclasse - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Frigid Explorer\n\nPagina: 21\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nBiting Cold\n\nDamage from your weapon attacks, Ranger spells, and Ranger features ignores XPHB to Cold damage.\n\nFrost Resistance\n\nYou have XPHB to Cold damage.\n\nPolar Strikes\n\nWhen you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon, you can deal an extra 1d4 Cold damage to the target, which can take this extra damage only once per turn. When you reach Ranger level 11, this extra damage increases to 1d6.\n\nNivel 3 - Hunter's Rime\n\nPagina: 21\n\nIce rimes you and your prey, protecting you and slowing them. When you cast XPHB, you gain XPHB equal to 1d10 plus your XPHB level.\n\nAdditionally, while a creature is marked by your XPHB, it can't take the XPHB action.\n\nNivel 3 - Winter Walker\n\nPagina: 21\n\nWithstand the Horrors of Frigid Wastelands\n\nWinter Walkers hone their craft in the bleak and frozen wilds of places like Icewind Dale. These ruthless, rimed Rangers hunt monsters that haunt arctic wastelands, eventually becoming frigid terrors themselves. Winter Walkers are well versed in the phenomena of Icewind Dale, including the latent magic of fallen Netherese cities, endemic monsters like XMM and SKT, and the rising threat of Underdark invaders. Due to their cold pragmatism, terrifying magic, and mastery of the region, Winter Walkers are regarded with equal parts respect and fear. Ten-Towns citizens say that Winter Walkers' frequent exposure to malignant entities gives them their fearsome powers. Many Reghed nomads, on the other hand, believe that nature spirits bestow on Winter Walkers a unique curse.\n\nNivel 3 - Winter Walker Spells\n\nPagina: 22\n\nWhen you reach a Ranger level specified in the Winter Walker Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nRanger Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB\n\nNivel 7 - Fortifying Soul\n\nPagina: 22\n\nYour experience surviving harrowing environments allows you to bolster your allies in addition to yourself. As a XPHB action, choose a number of creatures you can see equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one). Each chosen creature regains XPHB equal to 1d10 plus your Ranger level and has XPHB on saving throws to avoid or end the XPHB condition for 1 hour.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 11 - Chilling Retribution\n\nPagina: 22\n\nWhen a creature hits you with an attack roll, you can take a XPHB to force the creature to make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the target has the XPHB condition until the end of your next turn. While the target is XPHB, its XPHB is reduced to 0 feet.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 15 - Frozen Haunt\n\nPagina: 22\n\nWhen you cast XPHB, you can adopt a ghostly, snowy form. This form lasts until the spell ends, and while you are in this form, you gain the following benefits. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB unless you expend a level 4+ spell slot (no action required).\n\nFrozen Soul\n\nYou have XPHB to Cold damage. When you first adopt this form and at the start of each of your subsequent turns, each creature of your choice in a 15-foot XPHB originating from you takes 2d4 Cold damage.\n\nPartially Incorporeal\n\nYou have XPHB to the XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB conditions. You can move through creatures and objects as if they were XPHB, but you take 1d10 Force damage if you end your turn inside a creature or an object. If the form ends while you are inside a creature or an object, you are shunted to the nearest unoccupied space."},
  ["feature.winter-walker.frhof2014.ranger.winter-walker.3"]={title="Winter Walker",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nWithstand the Horrors of Frigid Wastelands\n\nWinter Walkers hone their craft in the bleak and frozen wilds of places like Icewind Dale. These ruthless, rimed Rangers hunt monsters that haunt arctic wastelands, eventually becoming frigid terrors themselves. Winter Walkers are well versed in the phenomena of Icewind Dale, including the latent magic of fallen Netherese cities, endemic monsters like XMM and SKT, and the rising threat of Underdark invaders. Due to their cold pragmatism, terrifying magic, and mastery of the region, Winter Walkers are regarded with equal parts respect and fear. Ten-Towns citizens say that Winter Walkers' frequent exposure to malignant entities gives them their fearsome powers. Many Reghed nomads, on the other hand, believe that nature spirits bestow on Winter Walkers a unique curse."},
  ["feature.winter-walker-spells.frhof2014.ranger.winter-walker.3"]={title="Winter Walker Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\nWhen you reach a Ranger level specified in the Winter Walker Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nRanger Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB"},
  ["creature.winter-wolf.mm2014"]={title="Winter Wolf",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 340\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant, Winter Wolf\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe wolf has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe wolf has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the wolf's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nSnow Camouflage\n\nThe wolf has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in snowy terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe wolf exhales a blast of freezing wind in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["language.winter-wolf.mm2014"]={title="Winter Wolf",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 340"},
  ["creature.winter-wolf.xmm2024"]={title="Winter Wolf",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 334\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe wolf has XPHB on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the wolf's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 12, each creature in a 15-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 18 (4d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["magicitem.winter-s-dark-bite.hftt2014"]={title="Winter's Dark Bite",subtitle="Item Magico - HftT - 2014",body="Pagina: 4\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nYou have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.\n\nThis greatsword is made of an unknown black metal. In most cases, it works as a +1 greatsword. But when used against a HftT, it works as a +3 greatsword. While in the Upside Down, it works as a +4 greatsword."},
  ["creature.wiri-fleagol.skt2014"]={title="Wiri Fleagol",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 176\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["spell.wish.phb2014"]={title="Wish",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 288\n\nWish is the mightiest spell a mortal creature can cast. By simply speaking aloud, you can alter the very foundations of reality in accord with your desires.\n\nThe basic use of this spell is to duplicate any other spell of 8th level or lower. You don't need to meet any requirements in that spell, including costly components. The spell simply takes effect. Alternatively, you can create one of the following effects of your choice:\n\n• You create one object of up to 25,000 gp in value that isn't a magic item. The object can be no more than 300 feet in any dimension, and it appears in an unoccupied space you can see on the ground.\n\n• You allow up to twenty creatures that you can see to regain all hit points, and you end all effects on them described in the greater restoration spell.\n\n• You grant up to ten creatures that you can see resistance to a damage type you choose.\n\n• You grant up to ten creatures you can see immunity to a single spell or other magical effect for 8 hours. For instance, you could make yourself and all your companions immune to a lich's life drain attack.\n\n• You undo a single recent event by forcing a reroll of any roll made within the last round (including your last turn). Reality reshapes itself to accommodate the new result. For example, a wish spell could undo an opponent's successful save, a foe's critical hit, or a friend's failed save. You can force the reroll to be made with advantage or disadvantage, and you can choose whether to use the reroll or the original roll.\n\nYou might be able to achieve something beyond the scope of the above examples. State your wish to the DM as precisely as possible. The DM has great latitude in ruling what occurs in such an instance; the greater the wish, the greater the likelihood that something goes wrong. This spell might simply fail, the effect you desire might only be partly achieved, or you might suffer some unforeseen consequence as a result of how you worded the wish. For example, wishing that a villain were dead might propel you forward in time to a period when that villain is no longer alive, effectively removing you from the game. Similarly, wishing for a legendary magic item or artifact might instantly transport you to the presence of the item's current owner.\n\nThe stress of casting this spell to produce any effect other than duplicating another spell weakens you. After enduring that stress, each time you cast a spell until you finish a long rest, you take 1d10 necrotic damage per level of that spell. This damage can't be reduced or prevented in any way. In addition, your Strength drops to 3, if it isn't 3 or lower already, for 2d4 days. For each of those days that you spend resting and doing nothing more than light activity, your remaining recovery time decreases by 2 days. Finally, there is a 33 chance that you are unable to cast wish ever again if you suffer this stress."},
  ["spell.wish.xphb2024"]={title="Wish",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 341\n\nWish is the mightiest spell a mortal can cast. By simply speaking aloud, you can alter reality itself.\n\nThe basic use of this spell is to duplicate any other spell of level 8 or lower. If you use it this way, you don't need to meet any requirements to cast that spell, including costly components. The spell simply takes effect.\n\nAlternatively, you can create one of the following effects of your choice:\n\n• Object Creation You create one object of up to 25,000 GP in value that isn't a magic item. The object can be no more than 300 feet in any dimension, and it appears in an unoccupied space that you can see on the ground.\n\n• Instant Health You allow yourself and up to twenty creatures that you can see to regain all XPHB, and you end all effects on them listed in the XPHB spell.\n\n• Resistance You grant up to ten creatures that you can see XPHB to one damage type that you choose. This XPHB is permanent.\n\n• Spell Immunity You grant up to ten creatures you can see immunity to a single spell or other magical effect for 8 hours.\n\n• Sudden Learning You replace one of your feats with another feat for which you are eligible. You lose all the benefits of the old feat and gain the benefits of the new one. You can't replace a feat that is a prerequisite for any of your other feats or features.\n\n• Roll Redo You undo a single recent event by forcing a reroll of any die roll made within the last round (including your last turn). Reality reshapes itself to accommodate the new result. For example, a Wish spell could undo an ally's failed saving throw or a foe's XPHB. You can force the reroll to be made with XPHB or XPHB, and you choose whether to use the reroll or the original roll.\n\n• Reshape Reality You may wish for something not included in any of the other effects. To do so, state your wish to the DM as precisely as possible. The DM has great latitude in ruling what occurs in such an instance; the greater the wish, the greater the likelihood that something goes wrong. This spell might simply fail, the effect you desire might be achieved only in part, or you might suffer an unforeseen consequence as a result of how you worded the wish. For example, wishing that a villain were dead might propel you forward in time to a period when that villain is no longer alive, effectively removing you from the game. Similarly, wishing for a Legendary magic item or an Artifact might instantly transport you to the presence of the item's current owner. If your wish is granted and its effects have consequences for a whole community, region, or world, you are likely to attract powerful foes. If your wish would affect a god, the god's divine servants might instantly intervene to prevent it or to encourage you to craft the wish in a particular way. If your wish would undo the multiverse itself, threaten the City of Sigil, or affect the Lady of Pain in any way, you see an image of her in your mind for a moment; she shakes her head, and your wish fails.\n\nThe stress of casting Wish to produce any effect other than duplicating another spell weakens you. After enduring that stress, each time you cast a spell until you finish a XPHB, you take 1d10 Necrotic damage per level of that spell. This damage can't be reduced or prevented in any way. In addition, your Strength score becomes 3 for 2d4 days. For each of those days that you spend resting and doing nothing more than light activity, your remaining recovery time decreases by 2 days. Finally, there is a 33 chance that you are unable to cast XPHB ever again if you suffer this stress."},
  ["spell.witch-bolt.phb2014"]={title="Witch Bolt",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 289\n\nA beam of crackling, blue energy lances out toward a creature within range, forming a sustained arc of lightning between you and the target. Make a ranged spell attack against that creature. On a hit, the target takes 1d12 lightning damage, and on each of your turns for the duration, you can use your action to deal 1d12 lightning damage to the target automatically. The spell ends if you use your action to do anything else. The spell also ends if the target is ever outside the spell's range or if it has Cover from you."},
  ["spell.witch-bolt.xphb2024"]={title="Witch Bolt",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 343\n\nA beam of crackling energy lances toward a creature within range, forming a sustained arc of lightning between you and the target. Make a ranged spell attack against it. On a hit, the target takes 2d12 Lightning damage.\n\nOn each of your subsequent turns, you can take a XPHB to deal 1d12 Lightning damage to the target automatically, even if the first attack missed.\n\nThe spell ends if the target is ever outside the spell's range or if it has Total XPHB from you."},
  ["optionalfeature.witch-sight.phb2014"]={title="Witch Sight",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nYou can see the true form of any shapechanger or creature concealed by illusion or transmutation magic while the creature is within 30 feet of you and within line of sight."},
  ["optionalfeature.witch-sight.xphb2024"]={title="Witch Sight",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 157\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 30 feet."},
  ["traphazard.witchbriars.nf2014"]={title="Witchbriars",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - NF - 2014",body="Some Low Netherese witches can enchant a patch of thorns to lash out at passersby. These enchanted thorn patches, called witchbriars, are often meant to ensnare Netherese mages who mistreat their workers, though witchbriars don't discriminate once they're animated. Witchbriars resemble an ordinary patch or hedge of thorny vines.\n\nA patch of witchbriars occupies a 10-foot XPHB and has AC 11; HP 30; and Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Psychic damage. When a creature casts a spell using a spell slot within 10 feet of witchbriars, thorny vines reach out to entwine the creature. The creature must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or have the XPHB condition (escape 14). Druids automatically succeed on this saving throw. While the target is Grappled in this way, it has the XPHB condition and takes 11 (2d10) Piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. One patch of witchbriars can grapple up to four creatures at a time.\n\nAny amount of Fire damage destroys a patch of witchbriars instantly."},
  ["creature.witchkite.mcv4ec2014"]={title="Witchkite",subtitle="Criatura - MCV4EC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 220 (21d12 + 84)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 15 | WIS 17 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nResistencias: fire, psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the witchkite fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe witchkite makes two Rend attacks and uses Malevolent Flare once.\n\nRend\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (3d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nMalevolent Flare\n\nThe witchkite spits magical, green-tinged flame at one creature it can see within 60 feet of itself. The target must make a 17 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 22 (5d8) fire damage and suffers one of the following effects of the witchkite's choice:\n\n• The target must use its reaction to make a melee attack against another creature of the witchkite's choice that is within the target's reach.\n\n• The target takes 13 (2d12) psychic damage.\n\nOn a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nEnchanting Gaze\n\nWhen a creature the witchkite can see moves within 10 feet of it, the witchkite emits an enchanting gaze at the creature. The creature must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or take 10 (3d6) psychic damage and have the charmed condition until the end of its next turn.\n\nRetribution\n\nImmediately after taking damage from a melee attack, the witchkite makes one Rend attack against the attacker."},
  ["background.witchlight-hand.wbtw2014"]={title="Witchlight Hand",subtitle="Background - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Carnival Fixture\n\nThe Witchlight Carnival provides you with free, modest lodging and food. In addition, you may wander about the carnival and partake of its many wonders at no cost to you, provided you don't disrupt its shows or cause any other trouble.\n\nCarnival Companion\n\nOver the years, you have earned the friendship of another carnival fixture. Roll a d8 and consult the Carnival Companion table to determine whom or what you've befriended, or you can choose an option that you like. Work with your DM to flesh out this friendship. This companion hangs around you while you're in the carnival, but it won't voluntarily leave the carnival.\n\nThe DM can use the WBtW stat block in WBtW to represent hands, performers, and animal trainers who serve as carnival companions. Statistics for the other companions appear in the MM.\n\nd8 | Companion\n\n1 | Old, cantankerous Witchlight hand\n\n2 | Young, impressionable Witchlight hand\n\n3 | Performer (such as an acrobat, a clown, or a musician)\n\n4 | Retired performer\n\n5 | Seasoned animal trainer\n\n6 | Old blink dog\n\n7 | Cheery sprite\n\n8 | Harmless, magical wisp of light (no stat block required) that has a flying speed of 30 feet, can hover, and sheds bright light in a 5-foot radius and dim light for an additional 5 feet\n\nCharacter Traits\n\nAs the players choose backgrounds for their characters, they can use the following tables to help determine their characters' personality traits, ideals, bonds, and flaws. Players can use these tables instead of the ones that appear in the PHB, or they can mix and match them. If a rolled result doesn't make sense for a character, the player can roll again or choose a more appropriate entry on the table.\n\nThese tables, while optional, are well suited to Feywild-themed adventures and are ideal for any character who has the feylost or Witchlight hand background.\n\nd8 | Trait\n\n1 | I'm haunted by fey laughter that only I can hear, though I know it's just my mind playing tricks on me.\n\n2 | Like a nomad, I can't settle down in one place for very long.\n\n3 | Good music makes me weep like a baby.\n\n4 | Wherever I go, I try to bring a little of the warmth and tranquility of home with me.\n\n5 | I have never lost my childlike sense of wonder.\n\n6 | When I have a new idea, I get wildly excited about it until I come up with another, better idea.\n\n7 | I live by my own set of weird and wonderful rules.\n\n8 | I can't bring myself to trust most adults.\n\nd8 | Ideal\n\n1 | Friendship. I never leave a friend behind. (Good)\n\n2 | Empathy. No creature should be made to suffer. (Good)\n\n3 | Wanderlust. I prefer to take the less traveled path. (Chaotic)\n\n4 | Changeability. Change is good, which is why I live by an ever-changing set of rules. (Chaotic)\n\n5 | Honor. A deal is a deal, and I would never break one. (Lawful)\n\n6 | Rule of Three. Everything in the multiverse happens in threes. I see the \"rule of three\" everywhere. (Lawful)\n\n7 | Obsession. I won't let go of a grudge. (Evil)\n\n8 | Greed. I will do whatever it takes to get what I want, regardless of the harm it might cause. (Evil)\n\nd8 | Bond\n\n1 | I would never break my word.\n\n2 | I find magic in all its forms to be compelling. The more magical a place, the more I am drawn to it.\n\n3 | I do what I can to protect the natural world.\n\n4 | A trusted friend is the most important thing in the multiverse to me.\n\n5 | I can't bring myself to harm a Fey creature, either because I consider myself one or because I fear the repercussions.\n\n6 | The Witchlight Carnival feels like home to me.\n\n7 | I'm drawn to the Feywild and long to return there, if only for a short while.\n\n8 | I feel indebted to WBtW and WBtW for giving me a home and a purpose.\n\nd8 | Flaw\n\n1 | I easily lose track of time. My poor sense of time means I'm always late.\n\n2 | I think the whole multiverse is out to get me.\n\n3 | I'm always operating under a tight timeline, and I'm obsessed with keeping everything on schedule.\n\n4 | I'm a kleptomaniac who covets shiny, sparkling treasure.\n\n5 | I'm forgetful. Sometimes I can't remember even the simplest things.\n\n6 | I never give away anything for free and always expect something in return.\n\n7 | I have many vices and tend to indulge them.\n\n8 | I'm always changing my mind—well, almost always."},
  ["creature.witchlight-hand-medium.wbtw2014"]={title="Witchlight Hand (Medium)",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any one language\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSecret Expertise\n\nThe hand has one of these additional skills: Acrobatics acrobatics 6, Animal Handling animal_handling 5, Arcana arcana 5, Athletics athletics 4, Medicine medicine 5, or Performance performance 5.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nPixie Dust (1/Day)\n\nThe hand sprinkles a pinch of pixie dust on itself or another creature it can see within 5 feet of it. The recipient gains a flying speed of 30 feet for 1 minute. If the creature is airborne when this effect ends, it falls safely to the ground, taking no damage and landing on its feet."},
  ["creature.witchlight-hand-small.wbtw2014"]={title="Witchlight Hand (Small)",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: S\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)"},
  ["magicitem.witchlight-vane.wbtw2014"]={title="Witchlight Vane",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis ornate rod is topped by a pair of butterfly wings and incorporates bits of red glass into its length. It weighs 3 pounds.\n\nMagic Weapon\n\nIn the hands of one who is attuned to it, the vane can be wielded as a magic mace that grants a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. In addition, the vane deals an extra 1d8 radiant damage on a hit.\n\nSense Mood\n\nWhile the vane is inside the perimeter of the Witchlight Carnival, it can sense the mood of every creature in the carnival that has an Intelligence of 4 or higher. As an action, a creature attuned to the vane can use it to pinpoint the location of the happiest creature in the carnival.\n\nThe butterfly shape at the top of the vane spins slowly clockwise when spirits in the carnival are generally high; if the general mood in the carnival is dour, the top of the vane spins slowly counterclockwise.\n\nSentience\n\nThe vane is a sentient, chaotic good wondrous item with an Intelligence of 11, a Wisdom of 14, and a Charisma of 14. It has hearing and normal vision out to a range of 30 feet, and it communicates by transmitting emotion to the creature attuned to it. Its purpose is to make sure everyone in the Witchlight Carnival is having a good time.\n\nAdditional Properties\n\nThe vane has the following additional properties:\n\n• The creature holding the vane has vulnerability to lightning damage.\n\n• The creature attuned to the vane can't be blinded, deafened, petrified, or stunned.\n\n• While carrying the vane, the creature attuned to it can cast the dancing lights, polymorph, or ray of frost spell as an action, requiring no spell components and using Charisma as the spellcasting ability. After the vane's polymorph spell is cast, roll a d8; on a roll of 3 or 8, the vane can't be used to cast this spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.witchlight-watch.wbtw2014"]={title="Witchlight Watch",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis ornate pocket watch is fastened to the end of a gold chain. It glows with a faint golden light when opened, and it makes a soft ticking noise that can be heard only by the creature holding it. The face of the watch shows a miniature painting of the Witchlight Carnival ringed by a tiny henge, orbited at night by a mote of light small enough to slip through the eye of a needle. This light causes the henge to cast shadows, and these shadows allow the watch's owner to track the passage of time.\n\nCarnival Setup and Takedown\n\nThe creature attuned to the watch can use an action to initiate the packing up or the unpacking of the Witchlight Carnival, provided the creature and the carnival are on the same plane of existence. In the span of 1 hour, all objects that are elements of the carnival are magically whisked about until everything is packed up and ready for travel, or unpacked and assembled. The watch has no effect on creatures, which can move about freely and safely while the carnival is being set up or taken down. Once the process of packing up or unpacking the carnival begins, it can't be stopped until the task is complete. When the watch is used to pack up or unpack the carnival, this property cannot be used again until 8 hours have elapsed.\n\nAdditional Properties\n\nThe pocket watch has the following additional properties:\n\n• While carrying the watch, the creature attuned to it can cast the fire bolt, invisibility, or message spell as an action, requiring no spell components and using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability. After the watch's invisibility spell is cast, roll a d8; on a roll of 3 or 8, the watch can't be used to cast this spell again until the next dawn.\n\n• The creature attuned to the watch gains 30 pounds. This extra weight vanishes when the attunement ends.\n\n• The creature attuned to the watch must eat and drink eight times the normal amount each day."},
  ["creature.witchstalker.mcv4ec2014"]={title="Witchstalker",subtitle="Criatura - MCV4EC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 82 (11d10 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe witchstalker has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSmell Magic\n\nThe witchstalker can sense the presence and location of magic within 120 feet of itself. It also has advantage on attack rolls against creatures that have cast a spell since the end of the witchstalker's last turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe witchstalker makes two Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (3d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nMind-Wracking Howl {@recharge 5}\n\nThe witchstalker unleashes a terrible howl, and each creature within 30 feet of it that isn't a Monstrosity must make a 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 24 (7d6) psychic damage and has disadvantage on Constitution saving throws to maintain concentration on spells until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSpell Stalk\n\nImmediately after a creature within 120 feet of the witchstalker casts a spell, the witchstalker magically teleports to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the creature and can make one Bite attack against the creature."},
  ["feature.withdraw-cost-1d6.xphb2024.rogue.base.5"]={title="Withdraw (Cost: 1d6)",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["spell.wither-and-bloom.au2014"]={title="Wither and Bloom",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 45\n\nYou invoke both death and life in a 10-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point within range. Each creature of your choice in that area makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 3d6 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. Nonmagical plants in that area that aren't creatures, such as trees and shrubs, wither.\n\nIn addition, one creature of your choice in that area can roll one of its unexpended XPHB and regain a number of XPHB equal to the roll plus your spellcasting ability modifier. That die is then expended."},
  ["spell.wither-and-bloom.scc2014"]={title="Wither and Bloom",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nYou invoke both death and life upon a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on a point within range. Each creature of your choice in that area must make a Constitution saving throw, taking 2d6 necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Nonmagical vegetation in that area withers.\n\nIn addition, one creature of your choice in that area can spend and roll one of its unspent Hit Dice and regain a number of hit points equal to the roll plus your spellcasting ability modifier."},
  ["creature.witherbloom-apprentice.scc2014"]={title="Witherbloom Apprentice",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 44 (8d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any two languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe apprentice regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point.\n\nVerdant Talisman\n\nAt the end of a 10-minute ritual, the apprentice can touch one willing creature (including itself) and bestow upon it a small talisman imbued with magic. Upon receiving the talisman, the creature gains 10 temporary hit points, and it can add 1d6 to its initiative rolls while it wears the talisman. These benefits last for 1 hour or until the apprentice conducts another ritual to bestow another talisman. When the benefits expire, the talisman crumbles to dust.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBriar Vine\n\nms 4 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) poison damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, the apprentice can pull it up to 10 feet closer to itself.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nWither Burst\n\nWhen the apprentice sees a creature within 30 feet of itself drop to 0 hit points, the apprentice channels the expended life essence and targets another creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 1 minute. While poisoned in this way, the target takes 3 (1d6) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.witherbloom-pledgemage.scc2014"]={title="Witherbloom Pledgemage",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 222\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 13 | INT 14 | WIS 17 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any two languages\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRegeneration\n\nAs long as the pledgemage has at least 1 hit point remaining, the pledgemage regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn.\n\nVerdant Talisman\n\nAt the end of a 10-minute ritual, the pledgemage can touch one willing creature (including itself) and bestow upon it a small talisman imbued with magic. Upon receiving the talisman, the creature gains 10 temporary hit points, and it can add 1d6 to its initiative rolls while it wears the talisman. These benefits last for 1 hour or until the pledgemage conducts another ritual to bestow another talisman. When the benefits expire, the talisman crumbles to dust.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBriar Vine\n\nms 5 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage plus 18 (4d8) poison damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, the apprentice can pull it up to 10 feet closer to itself.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nVociferous Form (1/Day)\n\nThe pledgemage transforms into an avatar of plants and shadow. While in this form, the pledgemage adds its Wisdom modifier to its AC if it isn't wearing armor or wielding a shield, and it has advantage on attack rolls against any creature missing hit points. This form lasts for 1 minute or until the pledgemage is reduced to 0 hit points.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nWither Burst\n\nWhen the pledgemage sees a creature within 30 feet of itself drop to 0 hit points, the pledgemage channels the expended life essence and targets another creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 1 minute. While poisoned in this way, the target takes 3 (1d6) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["magicitem.witherbloom-primer.scc2014"]={title="Witherbloom Primer",subtitle="Item Magico - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThe Witherbloom Primer is a magic textbook created at Strixhaven's Witherbloom College. The primer has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you make an Intelligence (Nature) or Wisdom (Survival) check while holding the primer, you can expend 1 charge to give yourself a 1d4 bonus to the check, immediately after you roll the d20.\n\nIn addition, if you study the primer at the end of a long rest, you can choose one 1st-level spell from the druid or wizard spell list. Before you finish your next long rest, you can cast the chosen spell once without a spell slot if you are holding the primer. Your spellcasting ability for this spell is your choice of Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma."},
  ["creature.witherbloom-professor-of-decay.scc2014"]={title="Witherbloom Professor of Decay",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 105 (14d8 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 16 | WIS 19 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any four languages\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEssence Transfer (1/Day)\n\nThe professor can cast the animate dead spell, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe professor makes two Mortality Spear attacks. It can replace one of the attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nMortality Spear\n\nms,rs 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h17 (3d8 + 4) necrotic damage, and the target can't regain hit points until the start of the professor's next turn.\n\nEssence Pulse {@recharge 5}\n\nThe professor creates a life-draining vortex in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on itself. Each creature of the professor's choice that it can see within that area must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 23 (5d8) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The professor then regains 10 hit points. An affected creature's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the necrotic damage taken. This reduction lasts until the creature finishes a long rest. The creature dies if its hit point maximum is reduced to 0."},
  ["creature.witherbloom-professor-of-growth.scc2014"]={title="Witherbloom Professor of Growth",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 16 | WIS 19 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any four languages\n\nResistencias: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe professor makes two Verdant Lash attacks.\n\nVerdant Lash\n\nms 7 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be pulled up to 10 feet closer to the professor.\n\nSummon Nature's Avatar (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe professor magically summons a Groff. The groff appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of the professor, acts as the professor's ally, and takes its turns immediately after the professor's. The professor can communicate telepathically with this groff while it remains. The groff remains for 10 minutes, until it or the professor dies, or until the professor dismisses it as an action."},
  ["background.witherbloom-student.scc2014"]={title="Witherbloom Student",subtitle="Background - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Witherbloom Initiate\n\nYou gain the SCC feat and must choose Witherbloom within it.\n\nIn addition, if you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic feature, the spells on the Witherbloom Spells table are added to the spell list of your spellcasting class. (If you are a multiclass character with multiple spell lists, these spells are added to all of them.)\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1st | Cure Wounds, Inflict Wounds\n\n2nd | Lesser Restoration, SCC\n\n3rd | Revivify, Vampiric Touch\n\n4th | Blight, Death Ward\n\n5th | Antilife Shell, Greater Restoration\n\nConsider customizing how your spells look when you cast them. Your Witherbloom spells might rely on material components or a spellcasting focus drawn from the swamp environment of Witherbloom, and your spells might take on an appearance suggesting those natural elements. Spectral shapes of swamp animals or plants might form amid your spell effects.\n\nBuilding a Witherbloom Character\n\nDruids and warlocks make up most of Witherbloom's student body. A few wizards (mostly those who study the PHB) and clerics (including those with the Divine Domains of PHB or PHB) also find their home in Witherbloom.\n\nA number of rangers and barbarians study at Witherbloom as well, and some rogues learn how to create and use poisons during their studies at this college.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nStudents of Witherbloom College are equally likely to be found picking herbs for a healing tincture or riding zombified swamp beasts through the bayou. The Witherbloom Personality Traits table suggests a variety of traits you might adopt for your character.\n\nd6 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I love brewing up a new recipe, even if some might be repulsed by my choice of ingredients. Or the final product. Or both.\n\n2 | My fashion sense is like my garden: withered, black, and weird.\n\n3 | I'm going to befriend every single monster in this swamp if it's the last thing I do.\n\n4 | Everything in this world dies eventually. The question is, what will you do with the time you have left?\n\n5 | I know we just met, but when you die, may I have your bones? For research.\n\n6 | Don't interrupt me; I'm brooding.\n\nWitherbloom Trinkets\n\nWhen you make your character, you may roll once on the SCC table, instead of on the phb in the PHB, for your starting trinket."},
  ["item.witherbloom-trinket.scc2014"]={title="Witherbloom Trinket",subtitle="Item - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWhen you make your character, you may roll once on the Witherbloom Trinkets table, instead of on the phb in the PHB, for your starting trinket.\n\nd6 | Trinket\n\n1 | A black bird-shaped mask, trimmed with glowing green thread\n\n2 | A set of rabbit bones\n\n3 | A pair of thick knee-high waders, stained with muck and moss\n\n4 | A slimy green tentacle, which occasionally wriggles\n\n5 | A notebook containing waterproof paper\n\n6 | A necklace of five small vials, each filled with luminescent white liquid"},
  ["creature.withers.toa2014"]={title="Withers",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 145\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages he knew in life\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nWithers carries the ToA.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, Withers has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nWithers makes two longsword attacks. He can use his Life Drain in place of one longsword attack.\n\nLife Drain\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) necrotic damage. The target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest. The target dies if this effect reduces its hit point maximum to 0.\n\nA humanoid slain by this attack rises 24 hours later as a zombie under the Withers's control, unless the humanoid is restored to life or its body is destroyed. Withers can have no more than twelve zombies under its control at one time.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage, or 7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage if used with two hands."},
  ["class.wizard.phb2014"]={title="Wizard",subtitle="Classe - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nArcane Recovery|Wizard||1\n\nSpellcasting|Wizard||1\n\nCantrip Formulas|Wizard||3|TCE\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard||4\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard||8\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard||12\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard||16\n\nSpell Mastery|Wizard||18\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard||19\n\nSignature Spells|Wizard||20\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA CLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Arcane Recovery\n\nPagina: 112\n\nYou have learned to regain some of your magical energy by studying your spellbook. Once per day when you finish a short rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your wizard level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 6th level or higher.\n\nFor example, if you're a 4th-level wizard, you can recover up to two levels worth of spell slots. You can recover either a 2nd-level spell slot or two 1st-level spell slots.\n\nNivel 1 - Arcane Recovery\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou can regain some of your magical energy by studying your spellbook. When you finish a XPHB, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level equal to no more than half your Wizard level (round up), and none of the slots can be level 6 or higher. For example, if you're a level 4 Wizard, you can recover up to two levels' worth of spell slots, regaining either one level 2 spell slot or two level 1 spell slots.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 1 - Ritual Adept\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou can cast any spell as a XPHB if that spell has the XPHB tag and the spell is in your spellbook. You needn't have the spell prepared, but you must read from the book to cast a spell in this way.\n\nNivel 1 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAs a student of arcane magic, you have a spellbook containing spells that show the first glimmerings of your true power. See PHB for the general rules of spellcasting and PHB for the spells.\n\nCantrips\n\nAt 1st level, you know three cantrips of your choice from the wizard spell list. You learn additional wizard cantrips of your choice at higher levels, as shown in the Cantrips Known column of the Wizard table.\n\nSpellbook\n\nAt 1st level, you have a spellbook containing six 1st-level spells of your choice. Your spellbook is the repository of the wizard spells you know, except your cantrips, which are fixed in your mind.\n\nPreparing and Casting Spells\n\nThe Wizard table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your wizard spells of 1st level and higher. To cast one of these spells, you must expend a slot of the spell's level or higher. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a long rest.\n\nYou prepare the list of wizard spells that are available for you to cast. To do so, choose a number of wizard spells from your spellbook equal to your Intelligence modifier + your wizard level (minimum of one spell). The spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nFor example, if you're a 3rd-level wizard, you have four 1st-level and two 2nd-level spell slots. With an Intelligence of 16, your list of prepared spells can include six spells of 1st or 2nd level, in any combination, chosen from your spellbook. If you prepare the 1st-level spell magic missile, you can cast it using a 1st-level or a 2nd-level slot. Casting the spell doesn't remove it from your list of prepared spells.\n\nYou can change your list of prepared spells when you finish a long rest. Preparing a new list of wizard spells requires time spent studying your spellbook and memorizing the incantations and gestures you must make to cast the spell: at least 1 minute per spell level for each spell on your list.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for your wizard spells, since you learn your wizard spells through dedicated study and memorization. You use your Intelligence whenever a spell refers to your spellcasting ability. In addition, you use your Intelligence modifier when setting the saving throw DC for a wizard spell you cast and when making an attack roll with one.\n\nSpell\n\nSpell\n\nRitual Casting\n\nYou can cast a wizard spell as a ritual if that spell has the ritual tag and you have the spell in your spellbook. You don't need to have the spell prepared.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an phb as a spellcasting focus for your wizard spells.\n\nLearning Spells of 1st Level and Higher\n\nEach time you gain a wizard level, you can add two wizard spells of your choice to your spellbook. Each of these spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots, as shown on the Wizard table. On your adventures, you might find other spells that you can add to your spellbook (see \"Your Spellbook\").\n\nYour Spellbook\n\nThe spells that you add to your spellbook as you gain levels reflect the arcane research you conduct on your own, as well as intellectual breakthroughs you have had about the nature of the multiverse. You might find other spells during your adventures. You could discover a spell recorded on a scroll in an evil wizard's chest, for example, or in a dusty tome in an ancient library.\n\nA spellbook doesn't contain cantrips.\n\nCopying a Spell into the Book\n\nWhen you find a wizard spell of 1st level or higher, you can add it to your spellbook if it is of a spell level you can prepare and if you can spare the time to decipher and copy it.\n\nCopying a spell into your spellbook involves reproducing the basic form of the spell, then deciphering the unique system of notation used by the wizard who wrote it. You must practice the spell until you understand the sounds or gestures required, then transcribe it into your spellbook using your own notation.\n\nFor each level of the spell, the process takes 2 hours and costs 50 gp. The cost represents material components you expend as you experiment with the spell to master it, as well as the fine inks you need to record it. Once you have spent this time and money, you can prepare the spell just like your other spells.\n\nCopying from a Spell Scroll\n\nA wizard spell on a spell scroll can be copied just as spells in spellbooks can be copied. When you copy a spell from a spell scroll, you must succeed on an Intelligence (Arcana) check with a DC equal to 10 + the spell's level. If the check succeeds, the spell is successfully copied. Whether the check succeeds or fails, the spell scroll is destroyed.\n\nReplacing the Book\n\nYou can copy a spell from your own spellbook into another book—for example, if you want to make a backup copy of your spellbook. This is just like copying a new spell into your spellbook, but faster and easier, since you understand your own notation and already know how to cast the spell. You need spend only 1 hour and 10 gp for each level of the copied spell.\n\nIf you lose your spellbook, you can use the same procedure to transcribe the spells that you have prepared into a new spellbook. Filling out the remainder of your spellbook requires you to find new spells to do so, as normal. For this reason, many wizards keep backup spellbooks in a safe place.\n\nThe Book's Appearance\n\nYour spellbook is a unique compilation of spells, with its own decorative flourishes and margin notes. It might be a plain, functional leather volume that you received as a gift from your master, a finely bound gilt-edged tome you found in an ancient library, or even a loose collection of notes scrounged together after you lost your previous spellbook in a mishap.\n\nNivel 1 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 165\n\nAs a student of arcane magic, you have learned to cast spells. See XPHB for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules with Wizard spells, which appear in the spells later in the class's description.\n\nCantrips\n\nYou know three Wizard cantrips of your choice. XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB are recommended. Whenever you finish a XPHB, you can replace one of your cantrips from this feature with another Wizard cantrip of your choice.\n\nWhen you reach Wizard levels 4 and 10, you learn another Wizard cantrip of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips column of the Wizard Features table.\n\nSpellbook\n\nYour wizardly apprenticeship culminated in the creation of a unique book: your spellbook. It is a Tiny object that weighs 3 pounds, contains 100 pages, and can be read only by you or someone casting XPHB. You determine the book's appearance and materials, such as a gilt-edged tome or a collection of vellum bound with twine.\n\nThe book contains the level 1+ spells you know. It starts with six level 1 Wizard spells of your choice. XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB are recommended.\n\nWhenever you gain a Wizard level after 1, add two Wizard spells of your choice to your spellbook. Each of these spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Wizard Features table. The spells are the culmination of arcane research you do regularly.\n\nSpell Slots\n\nThe Wizard Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a XPHB.\n\nPrepared Spells of Level 1+\n\nYou prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To do so, choose four spells from your spellbook. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nThe number of spells on your list increases as you gain Wizard levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Wizard Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Wizard spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 3 Wizard, your list of prepared spells can include six spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination, chosen from your spellbook.\n\nIf another Wizard feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Wizard spells for you.\n\nChanging Your Prepared Spells\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can change your list of prepared spells, replacing any of the spells there with spells from your spellbook.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for your Wizard spells.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an XPHB or your spellbook as a XPHB for your Wizard spells.\n\nExpanding and Replacing a Spellbook\n\nThe spells you add to your spellbook as you gain levels reflect your ongoing magical research, but you might find other spells during your adventures that you can add to the book. You could discover a Wizard spell on a XDMG, for example, and then copy it into your spellbook.\n\nCopying a Spell into the Book\n\nWhen you find a level 1+ Wizard spell, you can copy it into your spellbook if it's of a level you can prepare and if you have time to copy it. For each level of the spell, the transcription takes 2 hours and costs 50 GP. Afterward you can prepare the spell like the other spells in your spellbook.\n\nCopying the Book\n\nYou can copy a spell from your spellbook into another book. This is like copying a new spell into your spellbook but faster, since you already know how to cast the spell. You need spend only 1 hour and 10 GP for each level of the copied spell.\n\nIf you lose your spellbook, you can use the same procedure to transcribe the Wizard spells that you have prepared into a new spellbook. Filling out the remainder of the new book requires you to find new spells to do so. For this reason, many wizards keep a backup spellbook.\n\nNivel 2 - Arcane Tradition\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 2nd level, you choose an arcane tradition from the list of available traditions, shaping your practice of magic. Your choice grants you features at 2nd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.\n\nNivel 2 - Scholar\n\nPagina: 166\n\nWhile studying magic, you also specialized in another field of study. Choose one of the following skills in which you have proficiency: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB. You have XPHB in the chosen skill.\n\nNivel 2 - Scholar\n\nNivel 3 - Cantrip Formulas\n\nPagina: 75\n\n{@i 3rd-level wizard tce\n\nYou have scribed a set of arcane formulas in your spellbook that you can use to formulate a cantrip in your mind. Whenever you finish a long rest and consult those formulas in your spellbook, you can replace one wizard cantrip you know with another cantrip from the wizard spell list.\n\nNivel 3 - Wizard Subclass\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain a Wizard subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Wizard levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Wizard level or lower.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 4th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. You gain this feature again at Wizard levels 8, 12, and 16.\n\nNivel 5 - Memorize Spell\n\nPagina: 167\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can study your spellbook and replace one of the level 1+ Wizard spells you have prepared for your Spellcasting feature with another level 1+ spell from the book.\n\nNivel 6 - Arcane Tradition feature\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAt 6th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition.\n\nNivel 6 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain a feature from your Wizard Subclass.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 8th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 10 - Arcane Tradition feature\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAt 10th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition.\n\nNivel 10 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain a feature from your Wizard Subclass.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 12th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 14 - Arcane Tradition feature\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAt 14th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition.\n\nNivel 14 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain a feature from your Wizard Subclass.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 16th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 18 - Spell Mastery\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAt 18th level, you have achieved such mastery over certain spells that you can cast them at will. Choose a 1st-level wizard spell and a 2nd-level wizard spell that are in your spellbook. You can cast those spells at their lowest level without expending a spell slot when you have them prepared. If you want to cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot as normal.\n\nBy spending 8 hours in study, you can exchange one or both of the spells you chose for different spells of the same levels.\n\nNivel 18 - Spell Mastery\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou have achieved such mastery over certain spells that you can cast them at will. Choose a level 1 and a level 2 spell in your spellbook that have a casting time of an action. You always have those spells prepared, and you can cast them at their lowest level without expending a spell slot. To cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot.\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can study your spellbook and replace one of those spells with an eligible spell of the same level from the book.\n\nNivel 18 - Spell Mastery\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain an feats or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. XPHB is recommended.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nNivel 20 - Signature Spells\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 20th level, you gain mastery over two powerful spells and can cast them with little effort. Choose two 3rd-level wizard spells in your spellbook as your signature spells. You always have these spells prepared, they don't count against the number of spells you have prepared, and you can cast each of them once at 3rd level without expending a spell slot. When you do so, you can't do so again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nIf you want to cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot as normal.\n\nNivel 20 - Signature Spells\n\nPagina: 167\n\nChoose two level 3 spells in your spellbook as your signature spells. You always have these spells prepared, and you can cast each of them once at level 3 without expending a spell slot. When you do so, you can't cast them in this way again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB. To cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot.\n\nNivel 20 - Signature Spells"},
  ["class.wizard.xphb2024"]={title="Wizard",subtitle="Classe - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 164\n\nSpellcasting|Wizard|XPHB|1\n\nRitual Adept|Wizard|XPHB|1\n\nArcane Recovery|Wizard|XPHB|1\n\nScholar|Wizard|XPHB|2\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard|XPHB|4\n\nMemorize Spell|Wizard|XPHB|5\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard|XPHB|8\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard|XPHB|12\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Wizard|XPHB|16\n\nSpell Mastery|Wizard|XPHB|18\n\nEpic Boon|Wizard|XPHB|19\n\nSignature Spells|Wizard|XPHB|20\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA CLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Arcane Recovery\n\nPagina: 112\n\nYou have learned to regain some of your magical energy by studying your spellbook. Once per day when you finish a short rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your wizard level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 6th level or higher.\n\nFor example, if you're a 4th-level wizard, you can recover up to two levels worth of spell slots. You can recover either a 2nd-level spell slot or two 1st-level spell slots.\n\nNivel 1 - Arcane Recovery\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou can regain some of your magical energy by studying your spellbook. When you finish a XPHB, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level equal to no more than half your Wizard level (round up), and none of the slots can be level 6 or higher. For example, if you're a level 4 Wizard, you can recover up to two levels' worth of spell slots, regaining either one level 2 spell slot or two level 1 spell slots.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 1 - Ritual Adept\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou can cast any spell as a XPHB if that spell has the XPHB tag and the spell is in your spellbook. You needn't have the spell prepared, but you must read from the book to cast a spell in this way.\n\nNivel 1 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAs a student of arcane magic, you have a spellbook containing spells that show the first glimmerings of your true power. See PHB for the general rules of spellcasting and PHB for the spells.\n\nCantrips\n\nAt 1st level, you know three cantrips of your choice from the wizard spell list. You learn additional wizard cantrips of your choice at higher levels, as shown in the Cantrips Known column of the Wizard table.\n\nSpellbook\n\nAt 1st level, you have a spellbook containing six 1st-level spells of your choice. Your spellbook is the repository of the wizard spells you know, except your cantrips, which are fixed in your mind.\n\nPreparing and Casting Spells\n\nThe Wizard table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your wizard spells of 1st level and higher. To cast one of these spells, you must expend a slot of the spell's level or higher. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a long rest.\n\nYou prepare the list of wizard spells that are available for you to cast. To do so, choose a number of wizard spells from your spellbook equal to your Intelligence modifier + your wizard level (minimum of one spell). The spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nFor example, if you're a 3rd-level wizard, you have four 1st-level and two 2nd-level spell slots. With an Intelligence of 16, your list of prepared spells can include six spells of 1st or 2nd level, in any combination, chosen from your spellbook. If you prepare the 1st-level spell magic missile, you can cast it using a 1st-level or a 2nd-level slot. Casting the spell doesn't remove it from your list of prepared spells.\n\nYou can change your list of prepared spells when you finish a long rest. Preparing a new list of wizard spells requires time spent studying your spellbook and memorizing the incantations and gestures you must make to cast the spell: at least 1 minute per spell level for each spell on your list.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for your wizard spells, since you learn your wizard spells through dedicated study and memorization. You use your Intelligence whenever a spell refers to your spellcasting ability. In addition, you use your Intelligence modifier when setting the saving throw DC for a wizard spell you cast and when making an attack roll with one.\n\nSpell\n\nSpell\n\nRitual Casting\n\nYou can cast a wizard spell as a ritual if that spell has the ritual tag and you have the spell in your spellbook. You don't need to have the spell prepared.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an phb as a spellcasting focus for your wizard spells.\n\nLearning Spells of 1st Level and Higher\n\nEach time you gain a wizard level, you can add two wizard spells of your choice to your spellbook. Each of these spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots, as shown on the Wizard table. On your adventures, you might find other spells that you can add to your spellbook (see \"Your Spellbook\").\n\nYour Spellbook\n\nThe spells that you add to your spellbook as you gain levels reflect the arcane research you conduct on your own, as well as intellectual breakthroughs you have had about the nature of the multiverse. You might find other spells during your adventures. You could discover a spell recorded on a scroll in an evil wizard's chest, for example, or in a dusty tome in an ancient library.\n\nA spellbook doesn't contain cantrips.\n\nCopying a Spell into the Book\n\nWhen you find a wizard spell of 1st level or higher, you can add it to your spellbook if it is of a spell level you can prepare and if you can spare the time to decipher and copy it.\n\nCopying a spell into your spellbook involves reproducing the basic form of the spell, then deciphering the unique system of notation used by the wizard who wrote it. You must practice the spell until you understand the sounds or gestures required, then transcribe it into your spellbook using your own notation.\n\nFor each level of the spell, the process takes 2 hours and costs 50 gp. The cost represents material components you expend as you experiment with the spell to master it, as well as the fine inks you need to record it. Once you have spent this time and money, you can prepare the spell just like your other spells.\n\nCopying from a Spell Scroll\n\nA wizard spell on a spell scroll can be copied just as spells in spellbooks can be copied. When you copy a spell from a spell scroll, you must succeed on an Intelligence (Arcana) check with a DC equal to 10 + the spell's level. If the check succeeds, the spell is successfully copied. Whether the check succeeds or fails, the spell scroll is destroyed.\n\nReplacing the Book\n\nYou can copy a spell from your own spellbook into another book—for example, if you want to make a backup copy of your spellbook. This is just like copying a new spell into your spellbook, but faster and easier, since you understand your own notation and already know how to cast the spell. You need spend only 1 hour and 10 gp for each level of the copied spell.\n\nIf you lose your spellbook, you can use the same procedure to transcribe the spells that you have prepared into a new spellbook. Filling out the remainder of your spellbook requires you to find new spells to do so, as normal. For this reason, many wizards keep backup spellbooks in a safe place.\n\nThe Book's Appearance\n\nYour spellbook is a unique compilation of spells, with its own decorative flourishes and margin notes. It might be a plain, functional leather volume that you received as a gift from your master, a finely bound gilt-edged tome you found in an ancient library, or even a loose collection of notes scrounged together after you lost your previous spellbook in a mishap.\n\nNivel 1 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 165\n\nAs a student of arcane magic, you have learned to cast spells. See XPHB for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules with Wizard spells, which appear in the spells later in the class's description.\n\nCantrips\n\nYou know three Wizard cantrips of your choice. XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB are recommended. Whenever you finish a XPHB, you can replace one of your cantrips from this feature with another Wizard cantrip of your choice.\n\nWhen you reach Wizard levels 4 and 10, you learn another Wizard cantrip of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips column of the Wizard Features table.\n\nSpellbook\n\nYour wizardly apprenticeship culminated in the creation of a unique book: your spellbook. It is a Tiny object that weighs 3 pounds, contains 100 pages, and can be read only by you or someone casting XPHB. You determine the book's appearance and materials, such as a gilt-edged tome or a collection of vellum bound with twine.\n\nThe book contains the level 1+ spells you know. It starts with six level 1 Wizard spells of your choice. XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB are recommended.\n\nWhenever you gain a Wizard level after 1, add two Wizard spells of your choice to your spellbook. Each of these spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Wizard Features table. The spells are the culmination of arcane research you do regularly.\n\nSpell Slots\n\nThe Wizard Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a XPHB.\n\nPrepared Spells of Level 1+\n\nYou prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To do so, choose four spells from your spellbook. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nThe number of spells on your list increases as you gain Wizard levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Wizard Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Wizard spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 3 Wizard, your list of prepared spells can include six spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination, chosen from your spellbook.\n\nIf another Wizard feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Wizard spells for you.\n\nChanging Your Prepared Spells\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can change your list of prepared spells, replacing any of the spells there with spells from your spellbook.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for your Wizard spells.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an XPHB or your spellbook as a XPHB for your Wizard spells.\n\nExpanding and Replacing a Spellbook\n\nThe spells you add to your spellbook as you gain levels reflect your ongoing magical research, but you might find other spells during your adventures that you can add to the book. You could discover a Wizard spell on a XDMG, for example, and then copy it into your spellbook.\n\nCopying a Spell into the Book\n\nWhen you find a level 1+ Wizard spell, you can copy it into your spellbook if it's of a level you can prepare and if you have time to copy it. For each level of the spell, the transcription takes 2 hours and costs 50 GP. Afterward you can prepare the spell like the other spells in your spellbook.\n\nCopying the Book\n\nYou can copy a spell from your spellbook into another book. This is like copying a new spell into your spellbook but faster, since you already know how to cast the spell. You need spend only 1 hour and 10 GP for each level of the copied spell.\n\nIf you lose your spellbook, you can use the same procedure to transcribe the Wizard spells that you have prepared into a new spellbook. Filling out the remainder of the new book requires you to find new spells to do so. For this reason, many wizards keep a backup spellbook.\n\nNivel 2 - Arcane Tradition\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 2nd level, you choose an arcane tradition from the list of available traditions, shaping your practice of magic. Your choice grants you features at 2nd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.\n\nNivel 2 - Scholar\n\nPagina: 166\n\nWhile studying magic, you also specialized in another field of study. Choose one of the following skills in which you have proficiency: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB. You have XPHB in the chosen skill.\n\nNivel 2 - Scholar\n\nNivel 3 - Cantrip Formulas\n\nPagina: 75\n\n{@i 3rd-level wizard tce\n\nYou have scribed a set of arcane formulas in your spellbook that you can use to formulate a cantrip in your mind. Whenever you finish a long rest and consult those formulas in your spellbook, you can replace one wizard cantrip you know with another cantrip from the wizard spell list.\n\nNivel 3 - Wizard Subclass\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain a Wizard subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Wizard levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Wizard level or lower.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 4th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. You gain this feature again at Wizard levels 8, 12, and 16.\n\nNivel 5 - Memorize Spell\n\nPagina: 167\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can study your spellbook and replace one of the level 1+ Wizard spells you have prepared for your Spellcasting feature with another level 1+ spell from the book.\n\nNivel 6 - Arcane Tradition feature\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAt 6th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition.\n\nNivel 6 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain a feature from your Wizard Subclass.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 8th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 10 - Arcane Tradition feature\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAt 10th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition.\n\nNivel 10 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain a feature from your Wizard Subclass.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 12th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 14 - Arcane Tradition feature\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAt 14th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition.\n\nNivel 14 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain a feature from your Wizard Subclass.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 16th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 18 - Spell Mastery\n\nPagina: 112\n\nAt 18th level, you have achieved such mastery over certain spells that you can cast them at will. Choose a 1st-level wizard spell and a 2nd-level wizard spell that are in your spellbook. You can cast those spells at their lowest level without expending a spell slot when you have them prepared. If you want to cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot as normal.\n\nBy spending 8 hours in study, you can exchange one or both of the spells you chose for different spells of the same levels.\n\nNivel 18 - Spell Mastery\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou have achieved such mastery over certain spells that you can cast them at will. Choose a level 1 and a level 2 spell in your spellbook that have a casting time of an action. You always have those spells prepared, and you can cast them at their lowest level without expending a spell slot. To cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot.\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can study your spellbook and replace one of those spells with an eligible spell of the same level from the book.\n\nNivel 18 - Spell Mastery\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nPagina: 167\n\nYou gain an feats or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. XPHB is recommended.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nNivel 20 - Signature Spells\n\nPagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 20th level, you gain mastery over two powerful spells and can cast them with little effort. Choose two 3rd-level wizard spells in your spellbook as your signature spells. You always have these spells prepared, they don't count against the number of spells you have prepared, and you can cast each of them once at 3rd level without expending a spell slot. When you do so, you can't do so again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nIf you want to cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot as normal.\n\nNivel 20 - Signature Spells\n\nPagina: 167\n\nChoose two level 3 spells in your spellbook as your signature spells. You always have these spells prepared, and you can cast each of them once at level 3 without expending a spell slot. When you do so, you can't cast them in this way again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB. To cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot.\n\nNivel 20 - Signature Spells"},
  ["feature.wizard-subclass.xphb2024.wizard.base.3"]={title="Wizard Subclass",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 167\n\nYou gain a Wizard subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Wizard levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Wizard level or lower."},
  ["feature.wizardly-quill.tce2014.wizard.scribes.2"]={title="Wizardly Quill",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 77\n\n2nd-level Order of Scribes feature\n\nAs a bonus action, you can magically create a Tiny quill in your free hand. The magic quill has the following properties:\n\n• The quill doesn't require ink. When you write with it, it produces ink in a color of your choice on the writing surface.\n\n• The time you must spend to copy a spell into your spellbook equals 2 minutes per spell level if you use the quill for the transcription.\n\n• You can erase anything you write with the quill if you wave the feather over the text as a bonus action, provided the text is within 5 feet of you.\n\nThis quill disappears if you create another one or if you die."},
  ["creature.woe-strider.mot2014"]={title="Woe Strider",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 247\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 110 (13d10 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Cone\n\nThe woe strider's open mouth creates an area of antimagic, as in the antimagic field spell, in a 60-foot cone. At the start of each of its turns, the woe strider decides which way the cone faces and whether its mouth is open or closed.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe woe strider makes two claw attacks and one bite attack. If both claws hit the same creature, the target is grappled (escape 14).\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) psychic damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature that is grappled, incapacitated, or restrained. h13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) psychic damage. In addition, each magic item the creature is carrying that isn't an artifact has its magical properties suppressed for 1 minute."},
  ["creature.wolf.mm2014"]={title="Wolf",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 341\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe wolf has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe wolf has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the wolf's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 11 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["feature.wolf.phb2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.3"]={title="Wolf",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhile you're raging, your friends have advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature within 5 feet of you that is hostile to you. The spirit of the wolf makes you a leader of hunters."},
  ["feature.wolf.phb2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.6"]={title="Wolf",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nYou gain the hunting sensibilities of a wolf. You can track other creatures while traveling at a fast pace, and you can move stealthily while traveling at a normal pace."},
  ["feature.wolf.phb2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.14"]={title="Wolf",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhile you're raging, you can use a bonus action on your turn to knock a Large or smaller creature prone when you hit it with a melee weapon attack."},
  ["creature.wolf.xmm2024"]={title="Wolf",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 373\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe wolf has XPHB on attack rolls against a creature if at least one of the wolf's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.wolf-of-the-overworld.mcv3mc2014"]={title="Wolf of the Overworld",subtitle="Criatura - MCV3MC - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe wolf has advantage on attack rolls against a creature if at least one of the wolf's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the incapacitated condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit; reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 11 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition."},
  ["creature.wolf-in-sheep-s-clothing.qftis2014"]={title="Wolf-in-Sheep's-Clothing",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 9 | CON 16 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing is motionless (except for its lure) at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing move or act (except for the lure), that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing is animate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe wolf-in-sheep's-clothing makes one Bite attack and two Root Tentacle attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) acid damage.\n\nRoot Tentacle\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the grappled condition (escape 16). While grappled in this way, the target has the restrained condition, and at the start of each of the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing's turns, the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing can pull the target up to 10 feet toward itself (no action required). The wolf-in-sheep's-clothing has four root tentacles, each of which can grapple one target.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nCompletely Harmless Lure\n\nThe wolf-in-sheep's-clothing can change the color, texture, and shape of its lure to resemble a Tiny Beast or Tiny object. It can move the lure to reinforce the resemblance (no action required), but the lure must remain within 15 feet of the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing, connected by nearly invisible filament-like tendrils."},
  ["creature.wolfwere.mabjov2014"]={title="Wolfwere",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 12/13\n\nPV: 55 (10d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 8 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common (can't speak in wolf form)\n\nImunidades: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe wolfwere has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe wolfwere has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the wolfwere's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Hybrid form only)\n\nThe wolfwere makes two attacks: one with its Bite and one with its Claws.\n\nLongsword (Humanoid form only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage or 10 (1d10 + 5) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nBite (Wolf or Hybrid form only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nClaws (Hybrid form only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d4 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nLethargic Song (Humanoid form only)\n\nThe wolfwere plays a magical melody on an instrument. Every Humanoid within 200 feet of the wolfwere that hears the melody must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or be slowed for 10 minutes, as if the slow spell has been cast on them. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns. If a creature's saving throw is successful, the effect ends on it. A target that successfully saves is immune to this wolfwere's melody for the next 24 hours.\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe wolfwere polymorphs into a wolf-humanoid hybrid or into a Humanoid (elf or human), or back into its true form, which is a dire wolf. Its statistics, other than its AC, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies"},
  ["creature.wolfwere-alpha.mabjov2014"]={title="Wolfwere Alpha",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 12/13\n\nPV: 104 (16d8 + 32)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 8 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common (can't speak in wolf form)\n\nImunidades: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe wolfwere has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe wolfwere has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the wolfwere's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Hybrid form only)\n\nThe wolfwere makes three attacks: one with its Bite and two with its Claws.\n\nLongsword (Humanoid form only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage or 11 (1d10 + 6) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nBite (Wolf or Hybrid form only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nClaws (Hybrid form only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d4 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nLethargic Song (Humanoid form only)\n\nThe wolfwere plays a magical melody on an instrument. Every Humanoid within 200 feet of the wolfwere that hears the melody must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or be slowed for 10 minutes, as if the slow spell has been cast on them. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns. If a creature's saving throw is successful, the effect ends on it. A target that successfully saves is immune to this wolfwere's melody for the next 24 hours.\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe wolfwere polymorphs into a wolf-humanoid hybrid or into a Humanoid (elf or human), or back into its true form, which is a dire wolf. Its statistics, other than its AC, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies."},
  ["feature.wondrous-alteration.au2014.wizard.transmuter.3"]={title="Wondrous Alteration",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["reward.wongo.toa2014"]={title="Wongo",subtitle="Recompensa - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 129\n\n• Gender:\n\n• Alignment:\n\n• Personality:\n\n• Inherited flaw:\n\n• Enemy:\n\n• Power:"},
  ["creature.wood-elf.skt2014"]={title="Wood Elf",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish"},
  ["feat.wood-elf-magic.xge2024"]={title="Wood Elf Magic",subtitle="Feat - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 75\n\nYou learn the magic of the primeval woods, which are revered and protected by your people. You learn one druid cantrip of your choice. You also learn the longstrider and pass without trace spells, each of which you can cast once without expending a spell slot. You regain the ability to cast these two spells in this way when you finish a long rest. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for all three spells."},
  ["creature.wood-elf-wizard.cm2014"]={title="Wood Elf Wizard",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 187\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.wood-woad.mpmm2014"]={title="Wood Woad",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 266\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sylvan\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe wood woad has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring vegetation.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe wood woad regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it is in contact with the ground. If the wood woad takes fire damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the wood woad's next turn. The wood woad dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nTree Stride\n\nOnce on each of its turns, the wood woad can use 10 feet of its movement to step magically into one living tree within 5 feet of it and emerge from a second living tree within 60 feet of it that it can see, appearing in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the second tree. Both trees must be Large or bigger.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe wood woad makes two Club attacks.\n\nClub\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (4d4 + 4) force damage."},
  ["creature.wood-woad.vgm2014"]={title="Wood Woad",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sylvan\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Club\n\nIn the wood woad's hand, its club is magical and deals 7 (3d4) extra damage (included in its attacks).\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe wood woad has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring plant life.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe wood woad regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it is in contact with the ground. If the wood woad takes fire damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the wood woad's next turn. The wood woad dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nTree Stride\n\nOnce on each of its turns, the wood woad can use 10 feet of its movement to step magically into one living tree within 5 feet of it and emerge from a second living tree within 60 feet of it that it can see, appearing in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the second tree. Both trees must be Large or bigger.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe wood woad makes two attacks with its club.\n\nClub\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (4d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.woodcarver-s-tools.phb2014"]={title="Woodcarver's Tools",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWoodcarver's tools allow you to craft intricate objects from wood, such as wooden tokens or arrows.\n\nComponents\n\nWoodcarver's tools consist of a knife, a gouge, and a small saw.\n\nArcana, History\n\nYour expertise lends you additional insight when you examine wooden objects, such as figurines or arrows.\n\nNature\n\nYour knowledge of wooden objects gives you some added insight when you examine trees.\n\nRepair\n\nAs part of a short rest, you can repair a single damaged wooden object.\n\nCraft Arrows\n\nAs part of a short rest, you can craft up to five arrows. As part of a long rest, you can craft up to twenty. You must have enough wood on hand to produce them.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nCraft a small wooden figurine | 10\n\nCarve an intricate pattern in wood | 15"},
  ["item.woodcarver-s-tools.xphb2024"]={title="Woodcarver's Tools",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Dexterity\n\n• Utilize: Carve a pattern in wood (10)\n\n• Craft: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, Ranged weapons (except XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB), XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["creature.woodcrasher-baloth.psz2014"]={title="Woodcrasher Baloth",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 50"},
  ["magicitem.woodcutter-s-axe.wbtw2014"]={title="Woodcutter's Axe",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.\n\nWhen you use this axe to make an attack against a plant (an ordinary plant or a creature with the Plant type) or a wooden object that isn't being worn or carried, the attack deals an extra 2d6 slashing damage on a hit."},
  ["creature.wooden-donkey.wdmm2014"]={title="Wooden Donkey",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 84\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned"},
  ["item.wooden-staff.phb2014"]={title="Wooden Staff",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.wooden-staff.xphb2024"]={title="Wooden Staff",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 225\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["spell.word-of-radiance.xge2024"]={title="Word of Radiance",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 171\n\nYou utter a divine word, and burning radiance erupts from you. Each creature of your choice that you can see within range must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d6 radiant damage.\n\nThe spell's damage increases by 1d6 when you reach 5th level (2d6), 11th level (3d6), and 17th level (4d6)."},
  ["spell.word-of-radiance.xphb2024"]={title="Word of Radiance",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 343\n\nBurning radiance erupts from you in a 5-foot XPHB. Each creature of your choice that you can see in it must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d6 Radiant damage."},
  ["spell.word-of-recall.phb2014"]={title="Word of Recall",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 289\n\nYou and up to five willing creatures within 5 feet of you instantly teleport to a previously designated sanctuary. You and any creatures that teleport with you appear in the nearest unoccupied space to the spot you designated when you prepared your sanctuary (see below). If you cast this spell without first preparing a sanctuary, the spell has no effect.\n\nYou must designate a sanctuary by casting this spell within a location, such as a temple, dedicated to or strongly linked to your deity. If you attempt to cast the spell in this manner in an area that isn't dedicated to your deity, the spell has no effect."},
  ["spell.word-of-recall.xphb2024"]={title="Word of Recall",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 343\n\nYou and up to five willing creatures within 5 feet of you instantly teleport to a previously designated sanctuary. You and any creatures that teleport with you appear in the nearest unoccupied space to the spot you designated when you prepared your sanctuary (see below). If you cast this spell without first preparing a sanctuary, the spell has no effect.\n\nYou must designate a location, such as a temple, as a sanctuary by casting this spell there."},
  ["feature.words-of-creation.xphb2024.bard.base.20"]={title="Words of Creation",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 61\n\nYou have mastered two of the Words of Creation: the words of life and death. You therefore always have the XPHB and XPHB spells prepared. When you cast either spell, you can target a second creature with it if that creature is within 10 feet of the first target."},
  ["feature.words-of-terror.xge2024.bard.whispers.3"]={title="Words of Terror",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.worg.mm2014"]={title="Worg",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 341\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 26 (4d10 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 13 | INT 7 | WIS 11 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Goblin, Worg\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe worg has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["language.worg.mm2014"]={title="Worg",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 341"},
  ["creature.worg.xmm2024"]={title="Worg",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 335\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 26 (4d10 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 13 | INT 7 | WIS 11 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Goblin, Worg\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage, and the next attack roll made against the target before the start of the worg's next turn has XPHB."},
  ["language.worg.xmm2024"]={title="Worg",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 335"},
  ["creature.worker-robot.qftis2014"]={title="Worker Robot",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 9 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus the languages spoken by its creator\n\nResistencias: acid, fire\n\nImunidades: cold, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLightning Overload\n\nWhen the robot takes lightning damage, it must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw or have the stunned condition until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe robot makes two Cargo Tentacle attacks.\n\nCargo Tentacle\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the grappled condition (escape 15). The robot has two cargo tentacles, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nTractor Beam\n\nThe robot casts Telekinesis, targeting only creatures with the incapacitated condition or objects. It requires no spell components and uses Wisdom as the spellcasting ability."},
  ["magicitem.workshop-wrecker.au2014"]={title="Workshop Wrecker",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhen this 3-inch-diameter metal ball is activated as a XPHB action, it moves at a rapid speed, bouncing off walls and defying any attempts to capture it. The ball remains active for 1 minute or until you deactivate it by using a command word while within 30 feet of it (no action required). Once the ball is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nWhen you activate the ball and at the beginning of each of your turns while the ball is active, each creature in the area makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking Bludgeoning damage on a failed save. The save DC and amount of damage dealt depend on the approximate size of the area in which the ball is active, as shown on the following table.\n\nA nonmagical object that isn't being worn or carried also takes the damage if it is in the area. In confined areas larger than a 100-foot XPHB, the amount of damage caused by the ball is negligible. If the ball is activated in an unconfined area, it flies off in a random direction at a rate of 300 feet per round.\n\nArea | Save DC | Bludgeoning Damage\n\n15-foot XPHB | 18 | 6d6 + 5\n\n30-foot XPHB | 17 | 4d6 + 4\n\n50-foot XPHB | 15 | 2d6 + 2\n\n100-foot XPHB | 14 | 1d6 + 1"},
  ["creature.wraith.mm2014"]={title="Wraith",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 302\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 60\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 16 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe wraith can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the wraith has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLife Drain\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h21 (4d8 + 3) necrotic damage. The target must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest. The target dies if this effect reduces its hit point maximum to 0.\n\nCreate Specter\n\nThe wraith targets a humanoid within 10 feet of it that has been dead for no longer than 1 minute and died violently. The target's spirit rises as a specter in the space of its corpse or in the nearest unoccupied space. The specter is under the wraith's control. The wraith can have no more than seven specters under its control at one time."},
  ["creature.wraith.psz2014"]={title="Wraith",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.wraith.xmm2024"]={title="Wraith",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 336\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / S/M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 60\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 16 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus two other languages\n\nResistencias: acid, bludgeoning, cold, fire, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe wraith can move through other creatures and objects as if they were XPHB. It takes 5 (1d10) Force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the wraith has XPHB on ability checks and attack rolls.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLife Drain\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h21 (4d8 + 3) Necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, its XPHB maximum decreases by an amount equal to the damage taken.\n\nCreate Specter\n\nThe wraith targets a Humanoid corpse within 10 feet of itself that has been dead for no longer than 1 minute. The target's spirit rises as a XMM in the space of its corpse or in the nearest unoccupied space. The specter is under the wraith's control. The wraith can have no more than seven specters under its control at a time."},
  ["spell.wrath-of-nature.xge2024"]={title="Wrath of Nature",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 171\n\nYou call out to the spirits of nature to rouse them against your enemies. Choose a point you can see within range. The spirits cause trees, rocks, and grasses in a 60-foot cube centered on that point to become animated until the spell ends.\n\nGrasses and Undergrowth\n\nAny area of ground in the cube that is covered by grass or undergrowth is difficult terrain for your enemies.\n\nTrees\n\nAt the start of each of your turns, each of your enemies within 10 feet of any tree in the cube must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 4d6 slashing damage from whipping branches.\n\nRoots and Vines\n\nAt the end of each of your turns, one creature of your choice that is on the ground in the cube must succeed on a Strength saving throw or become restrained until the spell ends. A restrained creature can use an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nRocks\n\nAs a bonus action on your turn, you can cause a loose rock in the cube to launch at a creature you can see in the cube. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 3d8 nonmagical bludgeoning damage, and it must succeed on a Strength saving throw or fall prone."},
  ["feature.wrath-of-the-sea.xphb2024.druid.sea.3"]={title="Wrath of the Sea",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.wrath-of-the-storm.phb2014.cleric.tempest.1"]={title="Wrath of the Storm",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\nAlso at 1st level, you can thunderously rebuke attackers. When a creature within 5 feet of you that you can see hits you with an attack, you can use your reaction to cause the creature to make a Dexterity saving throw. The creature takes 2d8 lightning or thunder damage (your choice) on a failed saving throw, and half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.wrath-of-the-wild.rhw2014.ranger.hollow-warden.3"]={title="Wrath of the Wild",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["spell.wrathful-smite.phb2014"]={title="Wrathful Smite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 289\n\nThe next time you hit with a melee weapon attack during this spell's duration, your attack deals an extra 1d6 psychic damage. Additionally, if the target is a creature, it must make a Wisdom saving throw or be frightened of you until the spell ends. As an action, the creature can make a Wisdom check against your spell save DC to steel its resolve and end this spell."},
  ["spell.wrathful-smite.xphb2024"]={title="Wrathful Smite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 343\n\nThe target takes an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage from the attack, and it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition until the spell ends. At the end of each of its turns, the XPHB target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."},
  ["item.wreath-of-the-prism-awakened.egw2014"]={title="Wreath of the Prism (Awakened)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.wreath-of-the-prism-dormant.egw2014"]={title="Wreath of the Prism (Dormant)",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 274\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis loop of golden thorns is inset with dozens of gems representing the five colors of Tiamat.\n\nDormant\n\nWhile wearing the wreath in its dormant state, you have darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, wearing the wreath increases the range of your darkvision by 60 feet.\n\nWhen you hit a beast, dragon, or monstrosity of challenge rating 5 or lower with an attack, or when you grapple it, you can use the wreath to cast dominate monster on the creature (save 13). On a successful save, the target is immune to the power of the wreath for 24 hours. On a failure, a shimmering, golden image of the wreath appears as a collar around the target's neck or as a crown on its head (your choice) until it is no longer charmed by the spell. If you use the wreath to charm a second creature, the first spell immediately ends. When the spell ends, the target knows it was charmed by you."},
  ["item.wreath-of-the-prism-exalted.egw2014"]={title="Wreath of the Prism (Exalted)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.wretched-sorrowsworn.mpmm2014"]={title="Wretched Sorrowsworn",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 10 (4d6 - 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 12 | CON 9 | INT 5 | WIS 6 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nWretched Pack Tactics\n\nThe sorrowsworn has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the sorrowsworn's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated. The sorrowsworn otherwise has disadvantage on attack rolls.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d10 + 1) piercing damage, and the sorrowsworn attaches to the target. While attached, the sorrowsworn can't attack, and at the start of each of the sorrowsworn's turns, the target takes 6 (1d10 + 1) necrotic damage.\n\nThe attached sorrowsworn moves with the target whenever the target moves, requiring none of the sorrowsworn's movement. The sorrowsworn can detach itself by spending 5 feet of its movement on its turn. A creature, including the target, can use its action to detach the sorrowsworn."},
  ["spell.wristpocket.egw2014"]={title="Wristpocket",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 190\n\nYou flick your wrist, causing one object in your hand to vanish. The object, which only you can be holding and can weigh no more than 5 pounds, is transported to an extradimensional space, where it remains for the duration.\n\nUntil the spell ends, you can use your action to summon the object to your free hand, and you can use your action to return the object to the extradimensional space. An object still in the pocket plane when the spell ends appears in your space, at your feet."},
  ["feature.writhing-tide.tce2014.ranger.swarmkeeper.7"]={title="Writhing Tide",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.wrought-iron-tower.coa2014"]={title="Wrought-Iron Tower",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nConstructed from the same materials as his tower, Dispater's Wrought-Iron Tower is a powerful weapon that marks his rule over Dis. It embodies his ideals, representing defense, authority, and power. Its construction changes hourly, similar to the tower, appearing as either iron, steel, lead, or adamantine.\n\nThe Wrought-Iron Tower is a magic staff that functions as a warhammer and you have a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. If a creature is vulnerable to a certain type of damage, all damage dealt with the staff is converted to that damage type. When you hit a good aligned creature with it, that creature takes an extra 3d6 fire damage.\n\nWhile holding the staff, you can control and navigate through the Iron Tower in Dis. While the staff is on the layer of Dis, Dispater knows the exact location of it, and is capable of teleporting to within 30 feet of it at will.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Wrought-Iron Tower has the following random properties:\n\n• 2 dmg properties.\n\nThe Best Offense\n\nWhile attuned to the staff, you have a +2 bonus to AC and a +2 bonus to all saving throws.\n\nAdditionally, the staff has 10 charges. When you make an attack, you may spend 1 or more charges. For each charge spent, you deal an additional 2 fire damage on a successful attack. Charges are still consumed if the attack misses. The staff regains all charges each day at dawn.\n\nAfter dealing damage with the staff, you may use a bonus action and expend 1 charge to replace the damage dealt with your total AC instead.\n\nRulership\n\nThe Wrought-Iron Tower also functions as a Rod of Rulership, with an increased save DC of 18. This property costs 3 charges to use, though a creature that successfully saves against one of its uses is immune to future uses for 24 hours.\n\nSlag\n\nYou can cast Searing Smite at 6th level on yourself, expending 1 charge. Instead of doing fire damage, you may have Searing Smite inflict acid damage. The spell requires no concentration and lasts for 1 minute.\n\nDestroying the Staff\n\nThe Wrought-Iron Tower can only be destroyed inside the Iron Tower on Dis. Located somewhere within the tower is the forge that Dispater used to create the staff. An attuned creature must place the staff into the forge fires, then cast Dispel Evil and Good and touch the staff. They then take 20d10 fire damage, which ignores resistance and immunities. If the attuned creature survives the fire damage, the staff is destroyed."},
  ["item.wukka-nut.toa2014"]={title="Wukka Nut",subtitle="Item - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nThese fist-sized nuts grow on wukka trees, which are popular haunts for ToA, ToA, and ToA. A wukka nut rattles when shaken, causing its shell to shed bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. This magical light fades after 1 minute, but shaking the nut again causes the light to reappear. If the shell of the nut is cracked open, it loses its magic."},
  ["creature.wurm.ggr2014"]={title="Wurm",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 225\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 200 (16d12 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, burrow: 30\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 10 | CON 22 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 4\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe wurm deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nEarth Tremors\n\nThe wurm creates earth tremors as it moves overland or underground. Any creature that comes within 30 feet of the moving wurm for the first time on a turn must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or take 10 (3d6) bludgeoning damage and fall prone. Any structure or object anchored to the ground that comes within 30 feet of the moving wurm for the first time on a turn takes 10 (3d6) force damage.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe wurm can burrow through solid rock at half its burrow speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h24 (5d6 + 7) piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or be swallowed by the wurm. A swallowed creature is blinded and restrained, has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the wurm, and takes 17 (5d6) acid damage at the start of each of the wurm's turns. If the wurm takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the wurm must succeed on a 21 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, which fall prone in a space within 10 feet of the wurm. If the wurm dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can escape from the corpse by using 20 feet of movement, exiting prone."},
  ["creature.wurm.psk2014"]={title="Wurm",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.wurm.psz2014"]={title="Wurm",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.wyhan.dsotdq2014"]={title="Wyhan",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 79\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.wyllow.wdmm2014"]={title="Wyllow",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 70\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic, Elvish"},
  ["item.wyllow-s-staff-of-flowers.wdmm2014"]={title="Wyllow's Staff of Flowers",subtitle="Item - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 75"},
  ["creature.wynling.jttrc2014"]={title="Wynling",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / T\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 21 (6d4 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 20 | CON 13 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sylvan\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d4 + 5) bludgeoning damage.\n\nCloak of the Mountain {@recharge 4}\n\nThe wynling magically turns invisible, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, for 1 minute or until it makes an attack roll.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nTrickster's Flight\n\nImmediately after a creature the wynling can see misses the wynling with an attack roll, the wynling can move up to 30 feet. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks."},
  ["magicitem.wyrmreaver-gauntlets.bgg2014"]={title="Wyrmreaver Gauntlets",subtitle="Item Magico - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nOriginally crafted for ground-bound giant brawlers to fight against dragons and other enormous predators of the sky, these studded gauntlets are engraved with the dragon rune.\n\nWhile you are wearing these gauntlets, your unarmed strike deals an additional 1d6 force damage on a hit. Additionally, whenever you finish a long rest, choose one of the following damage types: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. You have resistance to the chosen damage type until you finish another long rest.\n\nInvoking the Runes\n\nAs a bonus action, you can invoke the gauntlets' runes and summon two enormous spectral fists that envelop the gauntlets and mimic your hand motions. The fists can also launch themselves to strike distant opponents, returning immediately to your space after they hit or miss.\n\nThe fists last for 1 minute or until you are incapacitated. While the spectral fists are active, unarmed strikes you make on your turn have a reach of 30 feet, and when you hit a creature with an opportunity attack made with your unarmed strike, the creature must succeed on a Strength saving throw (DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) or have the prone condition.\n\nOnce the runes have been invoked, they can't be invoked again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.wyrmskull-throne.skt2014"]={title="Wyrmskull Throne",subtitle="Item Magico - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nBuilt by dwarven gods and entrusted to the rulers of Shanatar, an ancient dwarven empire. The Wyrmskull Throne was a symbol of dwarven power and pride for ages untold. The throne hovers a foot off the ground and is a massive thing made of polished obsidian with oversized feet—the impaled skulls of four ancient blue dragons. Runes glisten in the carved obsidian winking to life with blue energy when the throne's powers are activated.\n\nAfter the fall of Shanatar, the Wyrmskull Throne fell into the clutches of less honorable creatures. A band of adventurers wrested the throne from the aquatic elf tyrant Gantar Kraok and sold it to the storm giant Neri for a considerable fortune. Neri had the throne magically enlarged and gave it to her husband, King Hekaton, as a gift, along with one of the Ruling Scepters of Shanatar, which she had found in a wreck at the bottom of the Trackless Sea. Only a creature attuned to a Ruling Scepter and in possession of it can harness the powers of the Wyrmskull Throne, which has become the centerpiece of King Hekaton's throne room in the undersea citadel of Maelstrom. Fear of the throne's power has helped prevent evil giants from challenging or threatening Hekaton's leadership.\n\nAny creature not attuned to a Ruling Scepter who sits on the throne is paralyzed and encased in a magical force field. While encased, the creature can't be touched or moved from the throne. Touching a Ruling Scepter to the force field dispels the field, though the creature remains paralyzed until it is separated from the throne.\n\nAny creature seated on the throne can hear faint Whispers in Draconic—the whisperings of four blue dragons whose skulls adorn the throne. Although powerless, these spirits try to influence the decisions of the throne's master.\n\nProperties of the Throne\n\nThe throne has 9 charges and regains all expended charges daily at dawn. A creature that sits on the throne while attuned to a Ruling Sceptor in its possession can harness the throne's properties, which are as follows:\n\nThe throne gains a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover and flies where the creature wills. This property doesn't expend any charges.\n\nBoth the throne and the creature sitting on it can move through earth and stone without disturbing the material they move through. This property doesn't expend any charges.\n\nAs an action, the creature can expend 1 charge to cast lightning bolt (spell save 19) from the throne. The spell is cast as though using a 9th-level spell slot and deals 49 (14d6) lightning damage. The bolt discharges from the mouth of one of the throne's blue dragon skulls.\n\nAs an action, the creature can expend 2 charges to cast the globe of invulnerability spell from the throne. The globe encloses both the creature and the throne.\n\nAs an action, the creature can expend 3 charges to create a spectral image of an ancient blue dragon that surrounds both it and the throne. The spectral dragon lasts for 1 minute. At the end of each of the creature's turns, the spectral dragon makes one bite attack and two claw attacks against targets of the creature's choice. These attacks have the same attack bonus, reach, and damage as an ancient blue dragon bite and claw attacks.\n\nDestroying the Throne\n\nThe Wyrmskull Throne can be destroyed by breaking at least five Ruling Scepters of Shanatar simultaneously on it. This fact has never been recorded or sung of among the dwarves or any bards or storytellers, and it can't be discovered with an ability check. Characters who want to destroy the throne must go on a quest to learn the method for doing so. The throne's destruction triggers an explosion, as shards of obsidian fly out in all directions. Each creature and object within a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on the throne must succeed on a 21 Dexterity saving throw, taking 70 (20d6) slashing damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.wyvern.mm2014"]={title="Wyvern",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 303\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 110 (13d10 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe wyvern makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its stinger. While flying, it can use its claws in place of one other attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nStinger\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage. The target must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 24 (7d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.wyvern.xmm2024"]={title="Wyvern",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 337\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 127 (15d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe wyvern makes one Bite attack and one Sting attack.\n\nBite\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nSting\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 24 (7d6) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the wyvern's next turn."},
  ["item.wyvern-poison.dmg2014"]={title="Wyvern Poison",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis poison must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated wyvern. A creature subjected to this poison must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 24 (7d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["item.wyvern-poison.xdmg2024"]={title="Wyvern Poison",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 91\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature subjected to Wyvern Poison makes a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 24 (7d6) Poison damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.x01.tofw2014"]={title="X01",subtitle="Criatura - ToFW - 2014",body="Pagina: 91\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.xalicas.egw2014"]={title="Xalicas",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\nThe Calamity took the lives of mortals and immortals alike. Many angels that fought with the Prime Deities were slain, and most that survived were wounded. The solar Xalicas, the right hand of the Arch Heart, was so injured that even the magic of the gods cannot help the angel regain the ability to see, fly, or leave Exandria. For over a century, Xalicas lay broken and blinded in the Greying Wildlands, moss and plants covering her body, until she had the strength to move, blaming herself for the small part she played in the Calamity.\n\nNow Xalicas wanders Wildemount to make up for the sins of the Calamity and prevent another devastating war. Her followers attempt to heal war-scarred lands and repair the natural world. Xalicas knows that alone and in her injured state she cannot stop all the evils in the world, so the angel lends her power to those she finds worthy: creatures who wish to stop unnecessary war, stand up to tyranny, and defend the innocent.\n\nAppearance\n\nXalicas is a silver-skinned solar who wears a clean white bandage around her eyes. Her body is covered in scars, and one of her wings is blackened and burned."},
  ["creature.xan-moonblade.mabjov2014"]={title="Xan Moonblade",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 13/16\n\nPV: 112 (25d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEnchanter\n\nWhen Xan casts hideous laughter, hold person, or suggestion, the target has disadvantage on the saving throw.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nXan has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put Xan to sleep.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nXan wields a Moonblade. The Moonblade has a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls (already factored into Xan's attacks) and has the finesse property.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nXan makes three Moonblade attacks.\n\nMoonblade\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) slashing damage or 11 (1d10 + 6) slashing damage if wielded with two hands, plus 7 (2d6) cold or fire damage (Xan's choice).\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nBladesong (1/Day)\n\nXan can use a bonus action to start a bladesong. His bladesong lasts for 1 minute. While using bladesong his movement increases to 40 ft., he gains a +3 bonus to his AC and he gains a +3 bonus to all concentration checks."},
  ["creature.xanathar.wdh2014"]={title="Xanathar",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.xandala.toa2014"]={title="Xandala",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 236\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 71 (11d8 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 18 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Elvish, Halfling\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nQuickened Spell (3/Day)\n\nWhen she casts a spell that has a casting time of 1 action, Xandala changes the casting time to 1 bonus action for that casting.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage, or 4 (1d8) bludgeoning damage when used with two hands."},
  ["creature.xarann-a-daragon.wdmm2014"]={title="Xarann A'Daragon",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 145\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Undercommon"},
  ["creature.xardorok-sunblight.idrotf2014"]={title="Xardorok Sunblight",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 287\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 93 (11d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDuergar Resilience\n\nXardorok has advantage on saving throws against poison, spells, and illusions, as well as to resist being charmed or paralyzed.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, Xardorok has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nXardorok attacks twice with a weapon or casts eldritch blast twice.\n\nSpiked Gauntlet\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage, or 8 (2d4 + 3) piercing damage while Xardorok is enlarged.\n\nEldritch Blast (Cantrip)\n\nrs 7 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature. h9 (1d10 + 4) force damage.\n\nEnlarge (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nFor 1 minute, Xardorok magically increases in size, along with anything he is wearing or carrying. While enlarged, Xardorok is Large, doubles his damage dice on Strength-based weapon attacks (included in his attacks), and makes Strength checks and Strength saving throws with advantage. If Xardorok lacks the room to become Large, he attains the maximum size possible in the space available.\n\nInvisibility {@recharge 4}\n\nXardorok magically turns invisible until he attacks, he casts a spell, he uses his Enlarge, or his concentration is broken (as if concentration on a spell). Any equipment Xardorok wears or carries is invisible with him.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nHellish Rebuke (2/Day)\n\nWhen Xardorok is damaged by a creature within 60 feet of him that he can see, the creature that damaged him is engulfed in hellish flames and must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 16 (3d10) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.xazax-the-eyemonger.oota2014"]={title="Xazax the Eyemonger",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 142\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.xelnene-thrul.aud2014"]={title="Xelnene Thrul",subtitle="Criatura - AUD - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 208 (32d8 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 21 | WIS 16 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEvocation Sculptor\n\nWhen Thrul casts a spell that creates an area of effect, she can choose herself and up to five other creatures she can see, sculpting the spell's energy around them. A chosen creature automatically succeeds on its saving throw against the spell, and it takes no damage if it would normally take half damage on a successful save.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThrul has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nProtective Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThrul makes four Arcane Burst attacks. She can replace two attacks with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 5 version) or XPHB (level 5 version).\n\nArcane Burst\n\nm,r 11, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h32 (5d10 + 5) Force damage."},
  ["item.xen-drik-trinket.erlw2014"]={title="Xen'drik Trinket",subtitle="Item - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 140\n\nRaridade: none\n\nd8 | Trinket\n\n1 | A punched ticket for a voyage from Sharn to Stormreach\n\n2 | A scorpion's barb engraved with a single Elvish letter\n\n3 | A copper coin so big you could use it as a dinner plate\n\n4 | An image of an elf warrior engraved on a giant's tooth\n\n5 | A single page from a giant wizard's spellbook, bearing an incomplete spell\n\n6 | A scrap of parchment, part of a map of Stormreach\n\n7 | A small book titled Feersome Beests of Zendrik\n\n8 | A scrimshaw carving of a sahuagin"},
  ["creature.xenk-yendar.hat-tg2014"]={title="Xenk Yendar",subtitle="Criatura - HAT-TG - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 157 (21d8 + 63)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Thayan, Undercommon\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Protection\n\nXenk and his allies within 10 feet of him have advantage on saving throws.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nXenk makes three Daggersword attacks and uses Daggersword Flourish. He can replace Daggersword Flourish with Cleansing Touch if it's available.\n\nDaggersword\n\nChoose the attack that corresponds to the daggersword's current form (see Daggersword Shift below):\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage if used with two hands, plus 6 (1d12) radiant damage.\n\nShortsword and Dagger\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 6 (1d12) radiant damage.\n\nDaggersword Flourish\n\nChoose the option that corresponds to the daggersword's current form (see Daggersword Shift below):\n\nLongsword\n\nXenk magically detaches the longsword's blade from its hilt, launching the blade at a creature he can see within 30 feet of himself. The target must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target is impaled by the blade, taking 14 (3d6 + 4) piercing damage, and is knocked prone. At the end of the current turn, the blade magically reattaches to its hilt.\n\nShortsword and Dagger\n\nXenk lashes out with both weapons. Each creature of his choice within 10 feet of him must make a 16 Dexterity throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 7 (2d6) piercing damage and has disadvantage on attack rolls until the start of Xenk's next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect.\n\nCleansing Touch (1/Day)\n\nXenk touches a creature within 5 feet of himself. The target magically regains 27 (6d8) hit points and gains the benefit of a lesser restoration spell.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDaggersword Shift\n\nXenk changes the form of his daggersword, choosing one of the following forms: a longsword, or a shortsword in one hand and a dagger in the other."},
  ["creature.xill.mff2014"]={title="Xill",subtitle="Criatura - MFF - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 18 | CON 13 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEthereal Jaunt\n\nAs a bonus action, a xill can magically shift from the Material Plane to the Ethereal Plane, or vice versa.\n\nPoison Stinger\n\nThe xill injects poison into one creature it hit with its claws this turn. The chosen creature must make a 11 Constitution saving throw, with disadvantage if the xill hit it more than once this turn, taking 14 (4d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one. If the poison damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target is stable but poisoned for 1 hour, even after regaining hit points, and is paralyzed while poisoned this way.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe xill makes four claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.xilonen.tftyp2014"]={title="Xilonen",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 83\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 2"},
  ["creature.xocopol.jttrc2014"]={title="Xocopol",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.xolkin-alassandar.skt2014"]={title="Xolkin Alassandar",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.xorn.mm2014"]={title="Xorn",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 304\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 73 (7d8 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, burrow: 20\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 22 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Terran\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEarth Glide\n\nThe xorn can burrow through nonmagical, unworked earth and stone. While doing so, the xorn doesn't disturb the material it moves through.\n\nStone Camouflage\n\nThe xorn has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.\n\nTreasure Sense\n\nThe xorn can pinpoint, by scent, the location of precious metals and stones, such as coins and gems, within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe xorn makes three claw attacks and one bite attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (3d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.xorn.xmm2024"]={title="Xorn",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 338\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 84 (8d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, burrow: 20\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 22 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft., Tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Terran)\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEarth Glide\n\nThe xorn can burrow through nonmagical, unworked earth and stone. While doing so, the xorn doesn't disturb the material it moves through.\n\nTreasure Sense\n\nThe xorn can pinpoint the location of precious metals and stones within 60 feet of itself.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe xorn makes one Bite attack and three Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h17 (4d6 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nCharge\n\nThe xorn moves up to its XPHB or XPHB straight toward an enemy it can sense."},
  ["creature.xorta.wdmm2014"]={title="Xorta",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 98\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.xot.crcotn2014"]={title="Xot",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: M"},
  ["creature.xvart.mpmm2014"]={title="Xvart",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 8 | WIS 7 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRaxivort's Tongue\n\nThe xvart can communicate with ordinary mm and mm, as well as mm and mm.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage. If at least one of the xvart's allies is within 5 feet of the target, the xvart can push the target 5 feet if the target is a Medium or smaller creature.\n\nSling\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLow Cunning\n\nThe xvart takes the Disengage action."},
  ["creature.xvart.vgm2014"]={title="Xvart",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 8 | WIS 7 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLow Cunning\n\nThe xvart can take the Disengage action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\nOverbearing Pack\n\nThe xvart has advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks to shove a creature if at least one of the xvart's allies is within 5 feet of the target and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nRaxivort's Tongue\n\nThe xvart can communicate with ordinary bats and rats, as well as giant bats and giant rats.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSling\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.xvart-speaker.vgm2014"]={title="Xvart Speaker",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 13 | WIS 7 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal and one additional language (usually Common or Goblin)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLow Cunning\n\nThe xvart can take the Disengage action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\nOverbearing Pack\n\nThe xvart has advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks to shove a creature if at least one of the xvart's allies is within 5 feet of the target and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nRaxivort's Tongue\n\nThe xvart can communicate with ordinary bats and rats, as well as giant bats and giant rats.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSling\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.xvart-warlock-of-raxivort.mpmm2014"]={title="Xvart Warlock of Raxivort",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 22 (5d6 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRaxivort's Blessing\n\nWhen the xvart reduces an enemy to 0 hit points, the xvart gains 4 temporary hit points.\n\nRaxivort's Tongue\n\nThe xvart can communicate with ordinary mm and mm, as well as mm and mm.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe xvart makes two Scimitar or Raxivort's Bite attacks.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nRaxivort's Bite\n\nrs 3 to hit, range 30 ft., one creature. h7 (1d10 + 2) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLow Cunning\n\nThe xvart takes the Disengage action."},
  ["creature.xvart-warlock-of-raxivort.vgm2014"]={title="Xvart Warlock of Raxivort",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 22 (5d6 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLow Cunning\n\nThe xvart can take the Disengage action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\nOverbearing Pack\n\nThe xvart has advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks to shove a creature if at least one of the xvart's allies is within 5 feet of the target and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nRaxivort's Tongue\n\nThe xvart can communicate with ordinary bats and rats, as well as giant bats and giant rats.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.xzar-the-chaos-clone.mabjov2014"]={title="Xzar the Chaos Clone",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 15/18\n\nPV: 121 (22d8 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 20 | WIS 10 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal, Primordial, Undercommon, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChaos Phage\n\nXzar's infusion with the Chaos Phage gives him the following benefits:\n\n• Xzar regains 10 hit points at the start of his turn if he has at least 1 hit point\n\n• Xzar has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects\n\n• Xzar has resistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n• Xzar has darkvision and telepathy to 60 feet\n\nGrim Harvest (1/Turn)\n\nWhen Xzar kills a creature that is neither a Construct nor Undead with a spell of 1st level or higher, Xzar regains hit points equal to twice the spell's level, or three times if it is a necromancy spell.\n\nNo Soul\n\nSince Xzar doesn't have a soul, resurrection magic is able to work upon him no matter how much time has passed. For example, the revivify spell would work on Xzar even a week after he died. However, spells like true resurrection and wish are unable to bring Xzar back to life if no body exists.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nXzar makes two Deprive attacks and uses Spellcasting.\n\nDeprive\n\nms,rs 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., or range 120 ft., one target. h27 (4d10 + 5) necrotic damage.\n\nDeath Eruption (1/Day)\n\nNegative energy erupts from Xzar, intensified by the Chaos Phage. Any creature in a 60-foot-radius sphere around Xzar (but not including Xzar) must make a 17 Constitution saving throw. A creature takes 36 (8d6) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A Humanoid killed by this ability rises at the start of Xzar's next turn as a zombie under his command."},
  ["creature.y.oota2014"]={title="Y",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 18"},
  ["creature.y-demi.scc2014"]={title="Y'demi",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 127 (15d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 20 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any four languages\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Aegis\n\nThe AC of Y'demi includes her Constitution modifier while she isn't wearing armor or wielding a shield.\n\nOriq Mask\n\nY'demi wears an Oriq mask. While wearing the mask, Y'demi can't be targeted by any divination magic or perceived through magical scrying sensors, and she adds double her proficiency bonus to Charisma (Deception) checks (included above).\n\nSanguine Sense\n\nWhile Y'demi isn't blinded, she can see any creature that isn't an Undead or a Construct within 60 feet of itself, even through Cover, Vision and Light areas, invisibility, or any other phenomena that would prevent sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nY'demi makes two Blood Lash attacks.\n\nBlood Lash\n\nms 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h21 (3d10 + 5) necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it can't regain hit points until the start of the Y'demi's next turn.\n\nBlood Boil {@recharge 4}\n\nY'demi chooses a point within 150 feet of itself, and a 20-foot radius sphere centered on that point fills with a burst of searing, blood-red mist. Each creature of Y'demi's choice that she can see in that area must make a 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 38 (7d10) necrotic damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a success, a creature takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated. A creature dies if reduced to 0 hit points by this necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSanguine Tentacles (1/Day)\n\nThe blood in the copper basin disappears as tentacles of congealed blood fill a 10-foot cube centered at a point on the ground that Y'demi can see within 15 feet of her. The effect lasts for 1 minute, during which time that area is difficult terrain. Any creature entering that area for the first time on a turn or starting its turn there must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or be restrained by the tentacles. A creature that starts its turn restrained by the tentacles takes 10 (3d6) bludgeoning damage. A creature restrained by the tentacles can use its action to make either a 13 Strength (Athletics) check or a 13 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check, ending the restrained condition on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.yagnoloth.mpmm2014"]={title="Yagnoloth",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 147 (14d10 + 70)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 14 | CON 21 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yagnoloth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yagnoloth makes one Electrified Touch attack and one Massive Arm attack, or it makes one Massive Arm attack and uses Battlefield Cunning, if available, or Teleport.\n\nElectrified Touch\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h27 (6d8) lightning damage.\n\nMassive Arm\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h23 (3d12 + 4) force damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or become stunned until the end of the yagnoloth's next turn.\n\nBattlefield Cunning {@recharge 4}\n\nUp to two allied yugoloths within 60 feet of the yagnoloth that can hear it can use their reactions to make one melee attack each.\n\nLife Leech\n\nThe yagnoloth touches one incapacitated creature within 15 feet of it. The target takes 36 (7d8 + 4) necrotic damage, and the yagnoloth gains temporary hit points equal to half the damage dealt. The target must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw, or its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to half the necrotic damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest, and the target dies if its hit point maximum is reduced to 0.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe yagnoloth teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.yagnoloth.mtf2014"]={title="Yagnoloth",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 252\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 147 (14d10 + 70)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 14 | CON 21 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yagnoloth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe yagnoloth's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yagnoloth makes one massive arm attack and one electrified touch attack, or it makes one massive arm attack and teleports before or after the attack.\n\nElectrified Touch\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h27 (6d8) lightning damage.\n\nMassive Arm\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h23 (3d12 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or is stunned until the end of the yagnoloth's next turn.\n\nLife Leech\n\nThe yagnoloth touches one incapacitated creature within 15 feet of it. The target takes 36 (7d8 + 4) necrotic damage, and the yagnoloth gains temporary hit points equal to half the damage dealt. The target must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw, or its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest, and the target dies if its hit point maximum is reduced to 0.\n\nBattlefield Cunning {@recharge 4}\n\nUp to two allied yugoloths within 60 feet of the yagnoloth that can hear it can use their reactions to make one melee attack each.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe yagnoloth magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.yagra-stonefist.wdh2014"]={title="Yagra Stonefist",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Orc\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRelentless Endurance\n\nWhen reduced to 0 hit points, Yagra drops to 1 hit point instead (but can't do this again until she finishes a long rest).\n\nPack Tactics\n\nYagra has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of her allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nSavage Attacks\n\nWhen she scores a critical hit Yagra can roll one of the weapon's damage dice and add it to the extra damage of the critical hit.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nYagra makes two melee attacks.\n\nMace\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 2 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h5 (1d10) piercing damage."},
  ["item.yahcha.toa2014"]={title="Yahcha",subtitle="Item - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA yahcha (pronounced YAH-chah) is a harmless, meaty beetle about the size of a human hand, which feeds on worms and maggots. It moves slowly (walking speed 10 feet) and is easy to catch. A creature with blue mist fever that eats a raw or cooked yahcha can immediately make a saving throw with advantage against that disease (see ToA page 40)."},
  ["creature.yak.skt2014"]={title="Yak",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.yakfolk-priest.skt2014"]={title="Yakfolk Priest",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 14 | WIS 18 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Yikaria\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPossession (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe yakfolk attempts to magically possess a humanoid or giant. The yakfolk must touch the target throughout a short rest, or the attempt fails. At the end of the rest, the target must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be possessed by the yakfolk, which disappears with everything it is carrying and wearing. Until the possession ends, the target is incapacitated, loses control of its body, and is unaware of its surroundings. The yakfolk now controls the body and can't be targeted by any attack, spell, or other effect, and it retains its alignment; its Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores; and its proficiencies. It otherwise uses the target's statistics, except the target's knowledge, class features, feats, and proficiencies.\n\nThe possession lasts until either the body drops to 0 hit points, the yakfolk ends the possession as an action, or the yakfolk is forced out of the body by an effect such as the dispel evil and good spell. When the possession ends, the yakfolk reappears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the body and is stunned until the end of its next turn. If the host body dies while it is possessed by the yakfolk, the yakfolk dies as well, and its body doesn't reappear.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yakfolk makes two melee attacks.\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage, or 12 (2d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\nSummon Earth Elemental (1/Day)\n\nThe yakfolk summons an earth elemental. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of its summoner and acts as an ally of the summoner. It remains for 10 minutes, until it dies, or until its summoner dismisses it as an action."},
  ["creature.yakfolk-warrior.skt2014"]={title="Yakfolk Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 60 (8d10 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 14 | WIS 15 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Yikaria\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPossession (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe yakfolk attempts to magically possess a humanoid or giant. The yakfolk must touch the target throughout a short rest, or the attempt fails. At the end of the rest, the target must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be possessed by the yakfolk, which disappears with everything it is carrying and wearing. Until the possession ends, the target is incapacitated, loses control of its body, and is unaware of its surroundings. The yakfolk now controls the body and can't be targeted by any attack, spell, or other effect, and it retains its alignment; its Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores; and its proficiencies. It otherwise uses the target's statistics, except the target's knowledge, class features, feats, and proficiencies.\n\nThe possession lasts until either the body drops to 0 hit points, the yakfolk ends the possession as an action, or the yakfolk is forced out of the body by an effect such as the dispel evil and good spell. When the possession ends, the yakfolk reappears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the body and is stunned until the end of its next turn. If the host body dies while it is possessed by the yakfolk, the yakfolk dies as well, and its body doesn't reappear.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yakfolk makes two attacks, either with its greatsword or its longbow.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 2 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h9 (2d8) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.yalaga-maladwyn.gos2014"]={title="Yalaga Maladwyn",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 226\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead"},
  ["creature.yalah-gralhund.wdh2014"]={title="Yalah Gralhund",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nINT 16\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal"},
  ["creature.yan-c-bin.pota2014"]={title="Yan-C-Bin",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / H\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 283 (21d12 + 147)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, fly: 150\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 24 | CON 24 | INT 16 | WIS 21 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Auran\n\nResistencias: cold, fire\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAir Form\n\nYan-C-Bin can enter a hostile creature's space and stop there. He can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing if air could pass through that space.\n\nEmpowered Attacks\n\nYan-C-Bin's slam attacks are treated as magical for the purpose of bypassing resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Yan-C-Bin fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYan-C-Bin has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nYan-C-Bin makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h20 (3d8 + 7) force damage plus 10 (3d6) lightning damage.\n\nThundercrack (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nYan-C-Bin unleashes a terrible thundercrack in a 100-foot-radius sphere centered on himself. All other creatures in the area must succeed on a 24 Constitution saving throw or take 31 (9d6) thunder damage and be deafened for 1 minute. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and is deafened until the start of Yan-C-Bin's next turn.\n\nChange Shape\n\nYan-C-Bin polymorphs into a Medium humanoid. While in polymorphed form, a swirling breeze surrounds him, his eyes are pale and cloudy, and he loses the Air Form trait. He can remain in polymorphed form for up to 1 hour. Reverting to his true form requires an action.\n\nSummon Elementals (1/Day)\n\nYan-C-Bin summons up to three air elemental and loses 30 hit points for each elemental he summons. Summoned elementals have maximum hit points, appear within 100 feet of Yan-C-Bin, and disappear if Yan-C-Bin is reduced to 0 hit points.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPeal of Thunder\n\nYan-C-Bin unleashes a peal of thunder that can be heard out to a range of 300 feet. Each creature within 30 feet of Yan-C-Bin takes 5 (1d10) thunder damage.\n\nTeleport (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nYan-C-Bin magically teleports up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space he can see. Anything Yan-C-Bin is wearing or carrying is teleported with him.\n\nSuffocate (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nYan-C-Bin steals the air of one breathing creature he can see within 60 feet of him. The target must make a 21 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target drops to 0 hit points and is dying. On a successful save, the target can't breathe or speak until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.yantha-coaxrock.oota2014"]={title="Yantha Coaxrock",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 138\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 16\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting"},
  ["creature.yanthdel-henlifel.pabtso2014"]={title="Yanthdel Henlifel",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 114\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.yarana.jttrc2014"]={title="Yarana",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 204\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.yarnspinner.dod2014"]={title="Yarnspinner",subtitle="Criatura - DoD - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / H\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 16 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 21 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic, Sylvan\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Rebirth\n\nIf Yarnspinner dies in his Domain of Delight, he revives with all his hit points 1d4 days later in a safe location in that domain.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Yarnspinner fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nYarnspinner can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nYarnspinner ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\nWeb Weaver (3/Day)\n\nYarnspinner can take 1 minute to craft one of the following structures out of webbing:\n\n• A 3-inch-thick, opaque wall of webbing consisting of up to three 10-foot-square sections, each of which must be anchored on at least two sides by other walls or surfaces. Each section has AC 12; 20 hit points; vulnerability to fire damage; and immunity to bludgeoning, poison, and psychic damage.\n\n• A hut small enough to fit in a 10-foot cube. The hut comes with a closable door and a comfortable bed made of webbing, sized for a Tiny, Small, or Medium creature.\n\n• A message consisting of no more than twenty-five characters, anchored at various points so it hangs in the air.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nYarnspinner makes two Bite attacks and uses Spellcasting or Web once.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (3d6 + 7) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) poison damage.\n\nWeb\n\nYarnspinner shoots webbing at one creature he can see within 120 feet of himself. The target must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or be restrained for 1 hour. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["item.yarting.frhof2014"]={title="Yarting",subtitle="Item - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.yarting.scag2014"]={title="Yarting",subtitle="Item - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA southern instrument from Amn and Calimshan that is a Faerûnian analog to the guitar. Numerous variations have spread across the continent."},
  ["deity.ye-cind.mtf2014"]={title="Ye'Cind",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["creature.yeenoghu.mpmm2014"]={title="Yeenoghu",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 270\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / H\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 333 (23d12 + 184)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 29 | DEX 16 | CON 26 | INT 16 | WIS 24 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Yeenoghu fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYeenoghu has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nYeenoghu makes three Flail attacks.\n\nFlail\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h22 (2d12 + 9) force damage. If it's his turn, Yeenoghu can cause the target to suffer one of the following additional effects, each of which he can apply only once per turn\n\n• Confusion The target must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or be affected by the confusion spell until the start of Yeenoghu's next turn.\n\n• Force The target takes an extra 13 (2d12) force damage.\n\n• Paralysis The target must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed until the start of Yeenoghu's next turn.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) acid damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRampage\n\nWhen Yeenoghu reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack, he moves up to half his speed and makes one Bite attack.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCharge\n\nYeenoghu moves up to his speed.\n\nSwat Away\n\nYeenoghu makes one Flail attack. If the attack hits, the target must succeed on a 24 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 15 feet in a straight line away from Yeenoghu. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the target is also knocked prone.\n\nSavage (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nYeenoghu makes a separate Bite attack against each creature within 10 feet of him."},
  ["creature.yeenoghu.mtf2014"]={title="Yeenoghu",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / H\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 333 (23d12 + 184)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 29 | DEX 16 | CON 26 | INT 15 | WIS 24 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Yeenoghu fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYeenoghu has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nYeenoghu's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nRampage\n\nWhen Yeenoghu reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on his turn, Yeenoghu can take a bonus action to move up to half his speed and make a bite attack.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nYeenoghu makes three flail attacks. If an attack hits, he can cause it to create an additional effect of his choice or at random (each effect can be used only once per Multiattack):\n\n1. The attack deals an extra 13 (2d12) bludgeoning damage.\n\n2. The target must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed until the start of Yeenoghu's next turn.\n\n3. The target must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or be affected by the confusion spell until the start of Yeenoghu's next turn.\n\nFlail\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (1d12 + 9) bludgeoning damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (1d10 + 9) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCharge\n\nYeenoghu moves up to his speed.\n\nSwat Away\n\nYeenoghu makes a flail attack. If the attack hits, the target must succeed on a 24 Strength saving throw or be pushed 15 feet in a straight line away from Yeenoghu. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the target falls prone.\n\nSavage (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nYeenoghu makes a bite attack against each creature within 10 feet of him."},
  ["item.yellow-death.fraif2014"]={title="Yellow Death",subtitle="Item - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature subjected to Yellow Death makes a 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 14 (4d6) Poison damage and has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only."},
  ["traphazard.yellow-mold.dmg2014"]={title="Yellow Mold",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 105\n\nYellow mold grows in dark places, and one patch covers a 5-foot square. If touched, the mold ejects a cloud of spores that fills a 10-foot cube originating from the mold. Any creature in the area must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or take 11 (2d10) poison damage and become poisoned for 1 minute. While poisoned in this way, the creature takes 5 (1d10) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a successful save.\n\nSunlight or any amount of fire damage instantly destroys one patch of yellow mold."},
  ["traphazard.yellow-mold.xdmg2024"]={title="Yellow Mold",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 79\n\nYellow mold grows in dark places, and one patch covers a 5-foot square. If touched, the mold ejects a cloud of spores that fills a 10-foot XPHB. Any creature in that area must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or take 11 (2d10) Poison damage and have the XPHB condition for 1 minute. While Poisoned in this way, the creature takes 5 (1d10) Poison damage at the start of each of its turns. The creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nDirect sunlight or any amount of Fire damage destroys a patch of yellow mold."},
  ["creature.yellow-musk-creeper.toa2014"]={title="Yellow Musk Creeper",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 6\n\nPV: 60 (11d8 + 11)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, climb: 5\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 3 | CON 12 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, exhaustion, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the creeper remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary flowering vine.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe creeper regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn. If the creeper takes fire, necrotic, or radiant damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of its next turn. The creeper dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTouch\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h13 (3d8) psychic damage. If the target is a humanoid that drops to 0 hit points as a result of this damage, it dies and is implanted with a yellow musk creeper bulb. Unless the bulb is destroyed, the corpse animates as a yellow musk zombie after being dead for 24 hours. The bulb is destroyed if the creature is raised from the dead before it can transform into a yellow musk zombie, or if the corpse is targeted by a remove curse spell or similar magic before it animates.\n\nYellow Musk (3/Day)\n\nThe creeper's flowers release a strong musk that targets all humanoids within 30 feet of it. Each target must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by the creeper for 1 minute. A creature charmed in this way does nothing on its turn except move as close as it can to the creeper. A creature charmed by the creeper can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.yellow-musk-zombie.toa2014"]={title="Yellow Musk Zombie",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 9 | CON 12 | INT 1 | WIS 6 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the zombie to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5 +the damage taken, unless the damage is fire or from a critical hit. On a success, the zombie drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.yellow-sapphire.dmg2014"]={title="Yellow Sapphire",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent fiery yellow or yellow-green gemstone."},
  ["item.yellow-sapphire.xdmg2024"]={title="Yellow Sapphire",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA fiery yellow or yellow green gemstone."},
  ["creature.yestabrod.oota2014"]={title="Yestabrod",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 233\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 15 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (1/Day)\n\nIf Yestabrod fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (3d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (3d4) poison damage.\n\nCaustic Spores (1/Day)\n\nYestabrod releases spores in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 12 Dexterity saving throw or take 1d6 acid damage at the start of each of Yestabrod's turns. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turn, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nInfestation Spores (1/Day)\n\nYestabrod releases spores that burst out in a cloud that fills a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on it, and the cloud lingers for 1 minute. Any flesh-and-blood creature in the cloud when it appears, or that enters it later, must make a 12 Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, the creature can't be infected by these spores for 24 hours. On a failed save, the creature is infected with a disease called the spores of Zuggtmoy and also gains a random form of indefinite madness (determined by rolling on the Madness of Zuggtmoy table in appendix D) that lasts until the creature is cured of the disease or dies. While infected in this way, the creature can't be reinfected, and it must be repeat the saving throw at the end of every 24 hours, ending the infection on a success. On a failure, the infected creature's body is slowly taken over by fungal growth, and after three such failed saves, the creature dies and is reanimated as a spore servant if it's a type of creature that can be (see the \"Myconids\" entry in the Monster Manual).\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCorpse Burst\n\nGore, offal, and acid erupt from a corpse within 20 feet of Yestabrod. Creatures within 10 feet of the corpse must succeed on a 12 Dexterity saving throw or take 7 (2d6) acid damage.\n\nFoul Absorption\n\nYestabrod absorbs putrescence from a corpse within 5 feet of it, regaining 1d8 + 2 hit points"},
  ["magicitem.yester-hill-axe.cos2014"]={title="Yester Hill Axe",subtitle="Item Magico - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThe axe's handle is carved with leaves and vines, and it weighs half as much as a normal battleaxe. When the axe hits a plant, whether an ordinary plant or a plant creature, the target takes an extra 1d8 slashing damage. When a creature of non-good alignment wields the axe, it sprouts thorns whenever its wielder makes an attack with it. These thorns prick the wielder for 1 piercing damage after the attack is made, and this damage is considered magical."},
  ["creature.yeth-hound.mpmm2014"]={title="Yeth Hound",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 271\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 51 (6d10 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common, Elvish and Sylvan but can't speak\n\nImunidades: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSunlight Banishment\n\nIf the yeth hound starts its turn in sunlight, it is transported to the Ethereal Plane. While sunlight shines on the spot from which it vanished, the hound must remain in the Deep Ethereal. After sunset, it returns to the Border Ethereal at the same spot, whereupon it typically sets out to find its pack or its master. The hound is visible on the Material Plane while it is in the Border Ethereal, and vice versa, but it can't affect or be affected by anything on the other plane. Once it is adjacent to its master or a pack mate that is on the Material Plane, a yeth hound in the Border Ethereal can return to the Material Plane as an action.\n\nTelepathic Bond\n\nWhile the yeth hound is on the same plane of existence as its master, it can magically convey what it senses to its master, and the two can communicate telepathically with each other.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage, plus 14 (4d6) psychic damage if the target is frightened.\n\nBaleful Baying\n\nThe yeth hound bays magically. Every enemy within 300 feet of the hound that can hear it must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened of the hound until the end of the hound's next turn or until the hound is incapacitated. A frightened target that starts its turn within 30 feet of the hound must use all its movement on that turn to get as far from the hound as possible, must finish the move before taking an action, and must take the most direct route, even if hazards lie that way. A target that successfully saves is immune to the baying of all yeth hounds for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.yeth-hound.vgm2014"]={title="Yeth Hound",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 51 (6d10 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common, Elvish, and Sylvan but can't speak\n\nImunidades: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe yeth hound has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\nSunlight Banishment\n\nIf the yeth hound starts its turn in sunlight, it is transported to the Ethereal Plane. While sunlight shines on the spot from which it vanished, the hound must remain in the Deep Ethereal. After sunset, it returns to the Border Ethereal at the same spot, whereupon it typically sets out to find its pack or its master. The hound is visible on the Material Plane while it is in the Border Ethereal, and vice versa, but it can't affect or be affected by anything on the other plane. Once it is adjacent to its master or a pack mate that is on the Material Plane, a yeth hound in the Border Ethereal can return to the Material Plane as an action.\n\nTelepathic Bond\n\nWhile the yeth hound is on the same plane of existence as its master, it can magically convey what it senses to its master, and the two can communicate telepathically with each other.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage, plus 14 (4d6) psychic damage if the target is frightened.\n\nBaleful Baying\n\nThe yeth hound bays magically. Every enemy within 300 feet of the hound that can hear it must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of the hound's next turn or until the hound is incapacitated. A frightened target that starts its turn within 30 feet of the hound must use all its movement on that turn to get as far from the hound as possible, must finish the move before taking an action, and must take the most direct route, even if hazards lie that way. A target that successfully saves is immune to the baying of all yeth hounds for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.yeti.mm2014"]={title="Yeti",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 305\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 51 (6d10 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Yeti\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear of Fire\n\nIf the yeti takes fire damage, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn.\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe yeti has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nSnow Camouflage\n\nThe yeti has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in snowy terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yeti can use its Chilling Gaze and makes two claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) cold damage.\n\nChilling Gaze\n\nThe yeti targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see the yeti, the target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw against this magic or take 10 (3d6) cold damage and then be paralyzed for 1 minute, unless it is immune to cold damage. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the target's saving throw is successful, or if the effect ends on it, the target is immune to the Chilling Gaze of all yetis (but not abominable yetis) for 1 hour."},
  ["language.yeti.mm2014"]={title="Yeti",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 305"},
  ["creature.yeti.xmm2024"]={title="Yeti",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 339\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 51 (6d10 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Yeti\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear of Fire\n\nIf the yeti takes Fire damage, it has XPHB on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yeti can use its Chilling Gaze and makes two attacks, using Claw or Ice Throw in any combination.\n\nClaw\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Cold damage.\n\nIce Throw\n\nr 6, range 30/120 ft. h6 (1d4 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 2 (1d4) Cold damage.\n\nChilling Gaze\n\ncon 13, one creature the yeti can see within 30 feet. actSaveFail 5 (2d4) Cold damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the yeti's next turn unless the target has XPHB to Cold damage. actSaveSuccess The target is immune to the Chilling Gaze of all yetis (but not abominable yetis) for 1 hour."},
  ["language.yeti.xmm2024"]={title="Yeti",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 339"},
  ["creature.yeti-leader.tftyp2014"]={title="Yeti Leader",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 183\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.yeti-tyke.idrotf2014"]={title="Yeti Tyke",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 313\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 6 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Yeti but can't speak\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe yeti has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nSnow Camouflage\n\nThe yeti has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in snowy terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) cold damage."},
  ["creature.yeti-tyke.mgelft2014"]={title="Yeti Tyke",subtitle="Criatura - MGELFT - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 6 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Yeti but can't speak\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe yeti tyke has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nSnow Camouflage\n\nThe yeti tyke has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in snowy terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) slashing damage, plus 2 (1d4) cold damage. Claw does both slashing and cold damage."},
  ["creature.yevgeni-krushkin.cos2014"]={title="Yevgeni Krushkin",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 100\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.yew-wand.phb2014"]={title="Yew Wand",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.yew-wand.xphb2024"]={title="Yew Wand",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 225\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.yggdrasti.mcv1sc2014"]={title="Yggdrasti",subtitle="Criatura - MCV1SC - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / G\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 112 (9d20 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, exhaustion\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCavities\n\nThe yggdrasti has 1d4 + 2 cavities in its trunk. Each cavity is big enough to hold one Medium creature, two Small creatures, or eight Tiny creatures. A creature inside a cavity has Cover against attacks and other effects that originate outside the cavity. The yggdrasti's cavities aren't connected to one another.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the yggdrasti is motionless and rooted in the ground at the start of combat, it looks just like a dead tree and has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the rooted yggdrasti move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the yggdrasti is animate.\n\nLightning Conduit\n\nIf the yggdrasti is subjected to lightning damage, it is unhurt, and the lightning damage is instead divided evenly among all creatures it is grappling. In addition, the yggdrasti regains one use of Lightning Discharge.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe yggdrasti doesn't require air or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yggdrasti makes two Root attacks and uses Lightning Discharge (if available).\n\nRoot\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a creature, it is grappled (escape 15). The yggdrasti has four roots, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nLightning Discharge (3/Day)\n\nThe yggdrasti shoots lightning at one creature within 120 feet of itself. The target must make a 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 31 (7d8) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.ygorl-lord-of-entropy.mff2014"]={title="Ygorl, Lord of Entropy",subtitle="Criatura - MFF - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 325 (26d10 + 182)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, swim: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 18 | CON 24 | INT 20 | WIS 16 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEntropic Aura\n\nEach creature that is not a construct or undead that ends its turn within 15 feet of Ygorl takes 14 (4d6) necrotic damage.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Ygorl fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYgorl has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nYgorl makes three attacks: two with its scythe, and one with its Entropic Touch.\n\nScythe\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h18 (2d10 + 7) slashing damage plus 19 (3d12) necrotic damage. Any creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack dies, with its body and everything it is wearing and carrying, except magic items, exploding into a cloud of ash. The creature can be restored to life only by means of a wish spell.\n\nEntropic Touch\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a 22 Constitution saving throw or gain one level of exhaustion.\n\nSummon Slaadi (1/Day)\n\nYgorl summons 1d4 + 1 death slaad. A summoned slaad appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of Ygorl, acts as an ally of Ygorl, and can't summon other slaadi. It remains for 1 minute, until it or Ygorl dies, or until Ygorl dismisses it as an action.\n\nTeleport\n\nYgorl teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nScythe\n\nYgorl makes one attack with its scythe.\n\nTeleport\n\nYgorl uses its Teleport action.\n\nCall the Void (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nEach creature that is not a construct or undead within 30 feet of Ygorl must make a 22 Constitution saving throw against the lord of entropy's attempt to unmake life, taking 42 (12d6) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Ygorl then regains a number of hit points equal to half the total damage taken by all affected creatures."},
  ["language.yikaria.skt2014"]={title="Yikaria",subtitle="Idioma - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 244"},
  ["creature.yinra-emberwind.egw2014"]={title="Yinra Emberwind",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 16 (3d8 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nYinra has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put her to sleep.\n\nKeen Hearing and Sight\n\nYinra has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.yithian.rhw2014"]={title="Yithian",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 281\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 180 (19d10 + 76)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 21 | WIS 18 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yithian has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nShielded Mind\n\nThe yithian's thoughts can't be read by any means, and other creatures can communicate with it telepathically only if it allows them.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nEldritch Magic (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yithian makes three Pincer attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Sup.\n\nPincer\n\nm 9, reach 10 ft. h18 (4d6 + 4) Piercing damage and the creature has the XPHB condition (escape 14).\n\nSup\n\nint 18, one creature within 10 feet that has the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB condition. actSaveFail 15 (3d6 + 5) Psychic damage. The target's XPHB maximum decreases by an amount equal to the damage taken, and the yithian regains XPHB equal to that amount.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nMind Swap {@recharge}\n\nint 18, one Humanoid the yithian can see within 5 feet. actSaveFail The target is possessed by the yithian; the yithian disappears, and the target has the XPHB condition and loses control of its body. The yithian now controls the body; the target has no awareness of the yithian's actions. The yithian can't be targeted by any attack, spell, or other effect. The yithian's game statistics are the same, except it uses the possessed target's XPHB and Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution modifiers. It knows everything the target knew.\n\nThe possession lasts until the body drops to 0 XPHB or the yithian leaves as a XPHB. When the possession ends, the yithian returns to its body, which appears within 5 feet of the target. The target is XPHB for 1 minute by alien memories, and it is immune to this yithian's Mind Swap for 24 hours. actSaveSuccess The target is immune to Mind Swap for 24 hours."},
  ["item.yklwa.toa2014"]={title="Yklwa",subtitle="Item - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA yklwa (pronounced YICK-ul-wah) is a simple melee weapon that is the traditional weapon of Chultan warriors. A yklwa consists of a 3-foot wooden shaft with a steel or stone blade up to 18 inches long. Although it has the thrown weapon property, the yklwa is not well balanced for throwing."},
  ["creature.yochlol.mm2014"]={title="Yochlol",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 65\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 136 (16d8 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 15 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Elvish, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe yochlol can use its action to polymorph into a form that resembles a female drow or giant spider, or back into its true form. Its statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yochlol has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe yochlol can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe yochlol ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yochlol makes two melee attacks.\n\nSlam (Bite in Spider Form)\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. (10 feet in demon form), one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning (piercing in spider form) damage plus 21 (6d6) poison damage.\n\nMist Form\n\nThe yochlol transforms into toxic mist or reverts to its true form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is also transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nWhile in mist form, the yochlol is incapacitated and can't speak. It has a flying speed of 30 feet, can hover, and can pass through any space that isn't airtight. It has advantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws, and it is immune to nonmagical damage.\n\nWhile in mist form, the yochlol can enter a creature's space and stop there. Each time that creature starts its turn with the yochlol in its space, the creature must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the start of its next turn. While poisoned in this way, the target is incapacitated."},
  ["creature.yochlol.xmm2024"]={title="Yochlol",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 341\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 153 (18d8 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 19 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Elvish, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDemonic Restoration\n\nIf the yochlol dies outside the Abyss, its body dissolves, and it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its XPHB in the Abyss.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yochlol has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe yochlol can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe yochlol ignores movement restrictions caused by webs.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yochlol makes two Caustic Lash attacks, and it can use Spellcasting to cast XPHB or XPHB if available.\n\nCaustic Lash\n\nm,r 8, reach 10 ft. or range 120 ft. h25 (6d6 + 4) Acid damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe yochlol shape-shifts into a Medium Humanoid or a Medium spider or back into its true form. Its game statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nToxic Escape\n\nactTrigger The yochlol is hit by an attack roll. actResponse The yochlol halves the attack's damage to itself (round down), and it teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of itself. con 15, each creature within 5 feet of the yochlol's destination space. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, it has the XPHB condition."},
  ["spell.yolande-s-regal-presence.xphb2024"]={title="Yolande's Regal Presence",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 343\n\nYou surround yourself with unearthly majesty in a 10-foot XPHB. Whenever the XPHB enters the space of a creature you can see and whenever a creature you can see enters the XPHB or ends its turn there, you can force that creature to make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 4d6 Psychic damage and has the XPHB condition, and you can push it up to 10 feet away. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only. A creature makes this save only once per turn."},
  ["deity.yondalla.mtf2014"]={title="Yondalla",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\nThe story of Yondalla begins at the dawn of the world, when halflings were timid wanderers, scraping out a meager existence. The goddess Yondalla took note of them and decided to adopt the halflings as her people. She was a strong leader with a vision for her people, and she dedicated her life to gathering them together and protecting them. Over time, she elevated to godhood those halflings who were the most adept at the skills halflings needed to survive. Those legendary halflings comprise the rest of the pantheon.\n\nYondalla created the first halfling villages and showed the people how to build, plant, and harvest. She knew that the bounty of a halfling village would be tempting plunder for any brigand or monster, so she used her powers to conceal their homes from easy discovery, blending them into the landscape so that most travelers would pass by without a second glance.\n\nTo the halflings, Yondalla is responsible for the spring in their step and the bubbly excitement they feel from knowing that luck is on their side. When a pumpkin grows to enormous size or a garden yields twice as many carrots as usual, credit goes to Yondalla. When a halfling trips, slides down a hillside, and lands on a nugget of gold, that's Yondalla turning bad luck into good."},
  ["deity.yondalla.phb2014"]={title="Yondalla",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["deity.yondalla.scag2014"]={title="Yondalla",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 23"},
  ["creature.yorb.toa2014"]={title="Yorb",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 108\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.yorn.wdh2014"]={title="Yorn",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Orc\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe thug has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the thug's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nRelentless Endurance (1/Day)\n\nWhen reduced to 0 hit points Yorn drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thug makes two melee attacks.\n\nMace\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 2 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h5 (1d10) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.young-amethyst-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Young Amethyst Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 161\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 168 (16d10 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: force, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nSingularity Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon creates a shining bead of gravitational force in its mouth, then releases the energy in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 17 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 36 (8d8) force damage, and its speed becomes 0 until the start of the dragon's next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced."},
  ["creature.young-amonkhet-dragon.psa2014"]={title="Young Amonkhet Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 6"},
  ["creature.young-basilisk.oota2014"]={title="Young Basilisk",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 100\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d6 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 15\n\nSTR 13\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPetrifying Gaze\n\nIf a creature starts its turn within 15 feet of the basilisk and the two of them can see each other, the basilisk can force the creature to make a 12 Constitution saving throw if the basilisk isn't incapacitated. On a failed save, the creature magically begins to turn to stone and is restrained. It must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn. On a success, the effect ends. On a failure, the creature is petrified until freed by the greater restoration spell or other magic.\n\nA creature that isn't surprised can avert its eyes to avoid the saving throw at the start of its turn. If it does so, it can't see the basilisk until the start of its next turn, when it can avert its eyes again. If it looks at the basilisk in the meantime, it must immediately make the save.\n\nIf the basilisk sees its reflection within 30 feet of it in bright light, it mistakes itself for a rival and targets itself with its gaze.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) poison damage."},
  ["creature.young-black-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Black Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 88\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 127 (15d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) acid damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales acid in a 30-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 49 (11d8) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-black-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Black Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 127 (15d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Acid damage.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 14, each creature in a 30-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 49 (14d6) Acid damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.young-blue-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Blue Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 91\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 152 (16d10 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) lightning damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales lightning in a 60-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 55 (10d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-blue-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Blue Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 152 (16d10 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 9, reach 10 ft. h12 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) Lightning damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 16, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 55 (10d10) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.young-brass-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Brass Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 105\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 110 (13d10 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Fire Breath\n\n• Sleep Breath"},
  ["creature.young-brass-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Brass Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 54\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 110 (13d10 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace two attacks with a use of Sleep Breath.\n\nRend\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 14, each creature in a 40-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 38 (11d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nSleep Breath\n\ncon 14, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, at which point it repeats the save. 2 The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. This effect ends for the target if it takes damage or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to wake it."},
  ["creature.young-bronze-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Bronze Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 108\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 142 (15d10 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Lightning Breath\n\n• Repulsion Breath"},
  ["creature.young-bronze-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Bronze Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 58\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 142 (15d10 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Repulsion Breath.\n\nRend\n\nm 8, reach 10 ft. h16 (2d10 + 5) Slashing damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 15, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 49 (9d10) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nRepulsion Breath\n\nstr 15, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target is pushed up to 40 feet straight away from the dragon and has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.young-bulette.pota2014"]={title="Young Bulette",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 139\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.young-cloud-giant.skt2014"]={title="Young Cloud Giant",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant"},
  ["creature.young-copper-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Copper Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 119 (14d10 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Acid Breath\n\n• Slowing Breath"},
  ["creature.young-copper-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Copper Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 78\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 119 (14d10 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Slowing Breath.\n\nRend\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 14, each creature in a 40-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 40 (9d8) Acid damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nSlowing Breath\n\ncon 14, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target can't take Reactions; its XPHB is halved; and it can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both. This effect lasts until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.young-crystal-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Young Crystal Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 95 (10d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 16 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, radiant\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d10 + 3) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) radiant damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nScintillating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a burst of brilliant radiance in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 27 (6d8) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The dragon then gains 10 temporary hit points by absorbing a portion of the radiant energy."},
  ["creature.young-deep-dragon.fraif2014"]={title="Young Deep Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 257\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 150 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage.\n\nNightmare Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nwis 14, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 22 (4d10) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the dragon's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.young-deep-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Young Deep Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 175\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 150 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) poison damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nNightmare Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a cloud of spores in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 22 (4d10) psychic damage, and it is frightened of the dragon for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage with no additional effects. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.young-dragon-turtle.ftd2014"]={title="Young Dragon Turtle",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 178 (17d12 + 68)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Draconic\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon turtle can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon turtle makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (1d12 + 5) piercing damage plus 6 (1d12) lightning damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nSteam Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon turtle exhales steam in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 42 (12d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Being underwater doesn't grant resistance against this damage."},
  ["creature.young-emerald-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Young Emerald Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 142 (15d10 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 19 | INT 16 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire, psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) psychic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nDisorienting Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of psychic dissonance in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 31 (9d6) psychic damage, and until the end of its next turn, when the creature makes an attack roll or an ability check, it must roll a d6 and reduce the total by the number rolled. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage with no additional effects."},
  ["creature.young-fire-giant.tftyp2014"]={title="Young Fire Giant",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nImunidades: fire"},
  ["creature.young-frost-giant.tftyp2014"]={title="Young Frost Giant",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 187\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nImunidades: cold"},
  ["creature.young-gold-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Gold Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 14 | CON 21 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Fire Breath\n\n• Weakening Breath"},
  ["creature.young-gold-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Gold Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 144\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 14 | CON 21 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Weakening Breath.\n\nRend\n\nm 10, reach 10 ft. h17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 17, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 55 (10d10) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nWeakening Breath\n\nstr 17, each creature that isn't currently affected by this breath in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target has XPHB on Strength-based XPHB and subtracts 3 (1d6) from its damage rolls. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically."},
  ["creature.young-green-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Green Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 136 (16d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nPoison Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales poisonous gas in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 42 (12d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-green-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Green Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 152\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 136 (16d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage.\n\nPoison Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 14, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 42 (12d6) Poison damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.young-griffon-medium.idrotf2014"]={title="Young Griffon (Medium)",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: M\n\nCR: 1\n\nPV: 32 (5d6 + 15)\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 16"},
  ["creature.young-griffon-small.idrotf2014"]={title="Young Griffon (Small)",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nPV: 13 (2d6 + 6)\n\nSTR 8"},
  ["creature.young-griffon-tiny.idrotf2014"]={title="Young Griffon (Tiny)",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: T\n\nCR: 0\n\nPV: 5 (1d4 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 2 | DEX 15 | CON 16"},
  ["creature.young-hill-giant.tftyp2014"]={title="Young Hill Giant",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant"},
  ["creature.young-hook-horror.oota2014"]={title="Young Hook Horror",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 11 (2d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 15, climb: 15\n\nSTR 12"},
  ["creature.young-horizonback-tortoise.crcotn2014"]={title="Young Horizonback Tortoise",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 68 (8d12 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\nIdiomas: understands Goblin but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe young horizonback tortoise can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.young-kraken.lr2014"]={title="Young Kraken",subtitle="Criatura - LR - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 207 (18d12 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 50\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 11 | CON 20 | INT 19 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Celestial, Infernal, Primordial, telepathy 60 ft. but can't speak\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, paralyzed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe kraken can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe kraken makes two tentacle attacks, each of which it can replace with one use of Fling.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h20 (3d8 + 7) piercing damage.\n\nIf the target is a Medium or smaller creature grappled by the kraken, that creature is swallowed and the grapple ends. While swallowed, the creature is blinded and restrained, it has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the kraken, and it takes 21 (6d6) acid damage at the start of each of the kraken's turns. One Medium or two smaller creatures can be swallowed at the same time.\n\nIf the kraken takes 35 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the kraken must succeed on a 23 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, which fall prone in spaces within 10 feet of the kraken. If the kraken dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can escape from the corpse using 10 feet of movement, exiting prone.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h17 (3d6 + 7) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 20). Until the grapple ends, the target is restrained. The kraken has ten tentacles, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nFling\n\nOne Medium or smaller object held or creature grappled by the kraken is thrown up to 40 feet in a random direction and knocked prone. If a thrown target strikes a solid surface, the target takes 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage for every 10 feet it was thrown. If the target is thrown at another creature, that creature must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or take the same damage and be knocked prone.\n\nLightning Strike\n\nThe kraken magically create a bolt of lightning, which can strike a target the kraken can see within 90 feet of it. The target must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-kruthik.mpmm2014"]={title="Young Kruthik",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10, climb: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Kruthik\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe kruthik has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the kruthik's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe kruthik can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 2½-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nStab\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.young-kruthik.mtf2014"]={title="Young Kruthik",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10, climb: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Kruthik\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe kruthik has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe kruthik has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the kruthik's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe kruthik can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 2½-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nStab\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.young-lunar-dragon.bam2014"]={title="Young Lunar Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 123 (13d10 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 240 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) cold damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a blast of frost in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the cone must make a 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 27 (6d8) cold damage, and its speed is halved until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nPhase (2/Day)\n\nThe dragon becomes partially incorporeal for as long as it maintains concentration on the effect (as if concentration on a spell). While partially incorporeal, the dragon has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage."},
  ["creature.young-moonstone-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Young Moonstone Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 144 (17d10 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Sylvan\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) radiant damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons:\n\n• Dream Breath The dragon exhales mist in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or fall unconscious for 10 minutes. This effect ends for a creature if the creature takes damage or someone uses an action to wake it.\n\n• Moonlight Breath The dragon exhales a beam of moonlight in a 60-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 38 (7d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-ogre-servant.tftyp2014"]={title="Young Ogre Servant",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 171\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant"},
  ["creature.young-purple-worm.pota2014"]={title="Young Purple Worm",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 113\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 13\n\nPV: 184 (15d20 + 90)"},
  ["creature.young-red-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Red Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 98\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) fire damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales fire in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 56 (16d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-red-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Red Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 254\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 10, reach 10 ft. h13 (2d6 + 6) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 17, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 56 (16d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.young-red-shadow-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Red Shadow Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 85\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLiving Shadow\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the dragon has resistance to damage that isn't force, psychic, or radiant.\n\nShadow Stealth\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the dragon can take the Hide action as a bonus action.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the dragon has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nShadow Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales shadowy fire in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 56 (16d6) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A humanoid reduced to 0 hit points by this damage dies, and an undead shadow rises from its corpse and acts immediately after the dragon in the initiative count. The shadow is under the dragon's control."},
  ["creature.young-remorhaz.mm2014"]={title="Young Remorhaz",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 17 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: cold, fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHeated Body\n\nA creature that touches the remorhaz or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 7 (2d6) fire damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h20 (3d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage."},
  ["creature.young-remorhaz.xmm2024"]={title="Young Remorhaz",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 258\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 20\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 17 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft., Tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: cold, fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHeat Aura\n\nAt the end of each of the remorhaz's turns, each creature in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the remorhaz takes 11 (2d10) Fire damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) Fire damage."},
  ["creature.young-sapphire-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Young Sapphire Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 157 (15d10 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 14 | CON 20 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe dragon can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) thunder damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nDebilitating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a pulse of high-pitched, nearly inaudible sound in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 33 (6d10) thunder damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated."},
  ["creature.young-sea-serpent.ftd2014"]={title="Young Sea Serpent",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 123 (13d12 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe sea serpent can breathe air and water.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe sea serpent deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sea serpent makes one Bite attack and one Constrict or Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) cold damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 20 ft., one creature. h22 (4d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is Large or smaller, it is grappled (escape 15). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the sea serpent can't constrict another target.\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 20 feet away and knocked prone.\n\nRime Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe sea serpent exhales a 30-foot cone of cold. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 38 (7d10) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-silver-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young Silver Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 168 (16d10 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Cold Breath\n\n• Paralyzing Breath"},
  ["creature.young-silver-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young Silver Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 278\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 168 (16d10 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Paralyzing Breath.\n\nRend\n\nm 10, reach 10 ft. h15 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 17, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 49 (11d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nParalyzing Breath\n\ncon 17, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. 1 The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, when it repeats the save. 2 The target has the XPHB condition, and it repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically."},
  ["creature.young-solar-dragon.bam2014"]={title="Young Solar Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 53\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 60\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 20 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe dragon doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and one Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) radiant damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage.\n\nPhotonic Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a flashing mote of radiant energy that travels to a point the dragon can see within 120 feet of itself, then blossoms into a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point. Each creature in the sphere must make a 17 Constitution saving throw, taking 44 (8d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-spirit-dragon.fraif2014"]={title="Young Spirit Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 277\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 152 (16d10 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 13 | CON 19 | INT 17 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Time-Warping Breath.\n\nRend\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h14 (3d6 + 4) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage.\n\nRuinous Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 15, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 36 (8d8) Necrotic damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nTime-Warping Breath\n\nwis 15, each creature that isn't currently affected by this breath in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target's XPHB is halved, it can't take Reactions, and it can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically."},
  ["creature.young-time-dragon.mpp2014"]={title="Young Time Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 210 (20d10 + 100)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 12 | CON 20 | INT 20 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic plus any four languages\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) force damage.\n\nTime Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of shimmering light in a 30-foot cone. Nonmagical objects and vegetation in that area that aren't being worn or carried crumble to dust. Each creature in that area must make a 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 31 (7d8) force damage and is magically weakened as it is desynchronized from the time stream. While the creature is in this state, attack rolls against it have advantage. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only. A weakened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself after it succeeds on two of these saves."},
  ["creature.young-topaz-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Young Topaz Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 127 (17d10 + 34)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d10 + 3) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nDesiccating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales yellowish necrotic energy in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 28 (8d6) necrotic damage and is weakened until the end of its next turn. A weakened creature has disadvantage on Strength-based ability checks and Strength saving throws, and the creature's weapon attacks that rely on Strength deal half damage. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't weakened."},
  ["creature.young-troglodyte.tftyp2014"]={title="Young Troglodyte",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 176\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.young-wereraven.cos2014"]={title="Young Wereraven",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 98\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: S\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)"},
  ["creature.young-white-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Young White Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 101\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 133 (14d10 + 56)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIce Walk\n\nThe dragon can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, difficult terrain composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) cold damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales an icy blast in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 45 (10d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.young-white-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Young White Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 328\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 123 (13d10 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIce Walk\n\nThe dragon can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, XPHB composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) Cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 15, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 40 (9d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.young-winter-wolf.tftyp2014"]={title="Young Winter Wolf",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.young-gi.jttrc2014"]={title="Young-Gi",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 85\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.yrlakka.wdmm2014"]={title="Yrlakka",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 202\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["magicitem.ythryn-mythallar.idrotf2014"]={title="Ythryn Mythallar",subtitle="Item Magico - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 316\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nA mythallar looks like an enormous crystal ball held in an ornate cradle. The globe sheds bright light in a 300-foot radius and dim light for an additional 300 feet. The globe draws magic from the Weave that can be harnessed for various purposes. For example, Netherese mages used mythallars to keep their cities aloft and empower their magic items. The bigger the mythallar, the more magic it can hold. The largest mythallars are 150 feet in diameter.\n\nThe Ythryn mythallar is a relatively small device—a mere 50 feet in diameter. To attune to this mythallar, a creature must finish a short rest within 30 feet of it, meditating on the mythallar. Up to eight creatures can be attuned to it at one time; otherwise, the Ythryn mythallar follows the attunement rules in the Dungeon Master's Guide. If a ninth creature tries to attune to the mythallar, nothing happens.\n\nAll creatures attuned to the Ythryn mythallar can sense when the device is being used. A creature attuned to the device can use any of its properties, but only if all other creatures attuned to the device agree to allow it. The Ythryn mythallar's properties are as follows:\n\n• While you're on the same plane of existence as the Ythryn mythallar, you can use an action to cause it to fly in any direction you choose at a speed of 30 feet. All matter within 500 feet of the device moves with it. The Ythryn mythallar and all structures held aloft by it hover in place when not in motion.\n\n• As an action, you can cause one magic item you are holding within 30 feet of the Ythryn mythallar to immediately regain all its expended charges or uses. A magic item recharged in this manner can't be recharged by the Ythryn mythallar again until after the item regains expended charges or uses on its own.\n\n• You can use the Ythryn mythallar to cast the control weather spell without requiring any components and without the need for you to be outdoors. This casting of the spell has a 50-mile radius. For the duration of the spell's casting time, you must be within 30 feet of the Ythryn mythallar or the spell fails.\n\nTouching the Mythallar\n\nAny creature that touches the globe of the mythallar must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 180 (20d10 + 70) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Undead have disadvantage on this saving throw. Any object that touches the globe, other than an artifact or the mythallar's cradle, is disintegrated instantly (no save)."},
  ["species.yuan-ti.mpmm2014"]={title="Yuan-Ti",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\nSize\n\nYou are Medium or Small. You choose the size when you select this race.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light and in darkness as if it were dim light. You discern colors in that darkness only as shades of gray.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against spells.\n\nPoison Resilience\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the poisoned condition on yourself. You also have resistance to poison damage.\n\nSerpentine Spellcasting\n\nYou know the poison spray cantrip. You can cast animal friendship an unlimited number of times with this trait, but you can target only snakes with it. Starting at 3rd level, you can also cast suggestion with this trait. Once you cast it, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have of 2nd level or higher.\n\nIntelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells when you cast them with this trait (choose when you select this race)."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-abomination.mm2014"]={title="Yuan-ti Abomination",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 308\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 127 (15d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 17 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe yuan-ti can use its action to polymorph into a Large snake, or back into its true form. Its statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It doesn't change form if it dies.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yuan-ti has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Abomination Form Only)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Abomination Form Only)\n\nThe yuan-ti makes two ranged attacks or three melee attacks, but can use its bite and constrict attacks only once each.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) poison damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 14). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the yuan-ti can't constrict another target.\n\nScimitar (Abomination Form Only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nLongbow (Abomination Form Only)\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) poison damage."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-abomination.xmm2024"]={title="Yuan-ti Abomination",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 345\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 127 (15d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 17 | WIS 18 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yuan-ti has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Yuan-ti Form Only)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yuan-ti makes two Bite attacks, and it can use Spellcasting to cast XPHB if available.\n\nBite\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nstr 15, one Large or smaller creature within 5 feet. actSaveFail 28 (7d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. The target has the XPHB condition (escape 14), and it has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\nPoison Spray {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 14, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 21 (6d6) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the yuan-ti's next turn. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe yuan-ti shape-shifts into a Large snake or returns to its true form. If it dies, it stays in its current form. The yuan-ti's game statistics are the same in each form, except where noted. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-anathema.mpmm2014"]={title="Yuan-ti Anathema",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 189 (18d12 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 13 | CON 19 | INT 19 | WIS 17 | CHA 20\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe anathema has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nOphidiophobia Aura\n\nAny creature of the anathema's choice, other than a snake or a yuan-ti, that starts its turn within 30 feet of the anathema must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of snakes and yuan-ti. A frightened target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a target's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the target is immune to this anathema's aura for the next 24 hours.\n\nSix Heads\n\nThe anathema has advantage on saves against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, or knocked unconscious.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Anathema Form Only)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Anathema Form Only)\n\nThe anathema makes two Claw attacks and one Flurry of Bites attack.\n\nClaw (Anathema Form Only)\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nFlurry of Bites (Anathema Form Only)\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h27 (6d6 + 6) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) poison damage.\n\nConstrict (Snake Form Only)\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 15 ft., one Large or smaller creature. h16 (3d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) acid damage, and the target is grappled (escape 16). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and it takes 16 (3d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) acid damage at the start of each of its turns. The anathema can constrict only one creature at a time.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe anathema transforms into a Huge constrictor snake or back into its true form. Its statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-anathema.vgm2014"]={title="Yuan-ti Anathema",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 202\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 189 (18d12 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 13 | CON 19 | INT 19 | WIS 17 | CHA 20\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., blindsight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe anathema has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nOphidiophobia Aura\n\nAny creature of the anathema's choice, other than a snake or a yuan-ti, that starts its turn within 30 feet of the anathema and can see or hear it must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of snakes and yuan-ti. A frightened target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a target's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the target is immune to this aura for the next 24 hours.\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe anathema can use its action to polymorph into a Huge giant constrictor snake, or back into its true form. its statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\nSix Heads\n\nThe anathema has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks and on saving throws against being blinded. charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, or knocked unconscious.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Anathema Form Only)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Anathema Form Only)\n\nThe anathema makes two claw attacks, one constrict attack, and one Flurry of Bites attack.\n\nClaw (Anathema Form Only)\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 15 ft., one Large or smaller creature. h16 (3d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) acid damage, and the target is grappled (escape 16). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained and takes 16 (3d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) acid damage at the start of each of its turns, and the anathema can't constrict another target.\n\nFlurry of Bites\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h27 (6d6 + 6) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) poison damage."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-broodguard.mpmm2014"]={title="Yuan-ti Broodguard",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 4\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nReckless\n\nAt the start of its turn, the broodguard can gain advantage on all melee weapon attack rolls it makes during that turn, but attack rolls against it have advantage until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe broodguard makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-broodguard.vgm2014"]={title="Yuan-ti Broodguard",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 203\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 4\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMental Resistance\n\nThe broodguard has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't paralyze it.\n\nReckless\n\nAt the start of its turn, the broodguard can gain advantage on all melee weapon attack rolls it makes during that turn, but attack rolls against it have advantage until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe broodguard makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-infiltrator.xmm2024"]={title="Yuan-ti Infiltrator",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 342\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 12 | CON 11 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yuan-ti has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yuan-ti makes two Scimitar attacks.\n\nScimitar\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage.\n\nPoison Ray\n\nr 4, range 120 ft. h9 (2d6 + 2) Poison damage."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-malison-type-1.mm2014"]={title="Yuan-ti Malison (Type 1)",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 309\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 14 | WIS 12 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe yuan-ti can use its action to polymorph into a Medium snake, or back into its true form. Its statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It doesn't change form if it dies.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yuan-ti has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMalison Type\n\nThe yuan-ti has one of the following types:\n\n• Type 1:\n\n• Type 2:\n\n• Type 3:\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Yuan-ti Form Only)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Yuan-ti Form Only)\n\nThe yuan-ti makes two ranged attacks or two melee attacks, but can use its bite only once.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage.\n\nScimitar (Yuan-ti Form Only)\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nLongbow (Yuan-ti Form Only)\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage."},
  ["creature.yuan-ti-malison-type-1.xmm2024"]={title="Yuan-ti Malison (Type 1)",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 343\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe yuan-ti has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Yuan-ti Form Only)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe yuan-ti makes two attacks, using Bite or Poison Ray in any combination, and it can use Spellcasting to cast XPHB if available.\n\nBite\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage.\n\nPoison Ray (Yuan-ti Form Only)\n\nr 5, range 120 ft. h12 (2d8 + 3) Poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe yuan-ti shape-shifts into a Medium snake or returns to its true form. If it dies, it stays in its current form. The yuan-ti's game statistics are the same in each form, except where noted. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
